! Cumulative lexicon for doc/fst-analyzer-plan.md's FST prototype. Grows
! one morpheme/mechanism at a time (e.g. "aki+nga", then "amit+juq", ...)
! as one lexicon rather than staying split into one file per word, so
! each new word's roots/affixes/rules are also checked against everything
! validated so far -- not just tested in isolation.
!
! Tag/canonical-text convention: a morpheme's own canonical form and its
! signature id are joined by a single "+" (Benoit's {surface:canonical/id}
! "/" role); "++" marks the boundary to the next morpheme (Benoit's "}{"
! role). Every morpheme -- root or affix -- echoes its own canonical text
! into the tag stream, even when (as with "nga" here) surface and canonical
! happen to be identical: keeping one uniform shape for every entry avoids
! a special-cased "sometimes the text is there, sometimes it isn't" rule
! that a future output-format conversion script would need to know about.
! See phonology.xfscript's header for why a bare "/" itself is avoided
! (xfst replace-rule context operator).
!
! lexc convention: upper side = analysis (root/affix + tags), lower side =
! pre-phonology intermediate form. This compiles as a *generator*; the
! analyser direction used by hfst-lookup is produced by composing with
! phonology.xfscript's rules and then inverting -- see that file's header
! for the exact build commands.

Multichar_Symbols +1n +1v +1vn +1nv +1nn +1c +1e +1a +1p +1q +1vv +2vn
  +tn-nom-s-4s +tn-dat-p +tv-ger-3p +tn-nom-p +tn-dat-s +tn-acc-p
  +tn-nom-p-4s +tn-loc-s +tn-abl-p +tn-gen-s +tn-loc-p +tn-acc-s
  +tn-dat-p-4s +tv-ger-1s +tv-dec-1s +tn-via-p +tv-part-1s-3s-prespas
  +2vv +tn-abl-p-4s +tv-part-1s-3p-prespas +2nn +tn-loc-p-4s +2nv
  +tv-dec-1p +tn-nom-s-4p +tv-ger-1p +tv-caus-1s +tv-caus-1p +tv-caus-2s
  +tv-ger-2s +tn-sim-p +tv-imp-2s +tv-caus-4s +tn-via-s-4s +tn-nom-d
  +tv-part-1s-3s-fut +tv-dec-3s +tv-part-3p +&iq +tn-abl-s
  ++ SUPPR VVNG NASAL PMARK DECAP VOICE MINSERT TNNOMD JGUARD KGUARD

LEXICON Root
Nouns ;
Verbs ;
Conjunctions ;
Exclamations ;
Adverbs ;
Pronouns ;

! Bulk-generated roots (tools/fst/generate_roots.py, from RootsSpalding.csv/
! RootsSchneider.csv/Pronouns.csv) live in separately-named lexicons, not
! merged into the hand-picked ones above: hfst-lexc refuses to compile the
! same LEXICON name defined across two files ("Sublexicon defined more than
! once"). Each one converges on the same downstream continuation lexicons
! as its hand-picked counterpart (e.g. NounsGenerated's entries -> the same
! NounContinuations as Nouns's), so a generated root reaches every
! applicable suffix/ending class exactly like a hand-picked one does.
NounsGenerated ;
VerbsGenerated ;
ConjunctionsGenerated ;
ExclamationsGenerated ;
AdverbsGenerated ;
PronounsGenerated ;
DemonstrativeAdverbsGenerated ;
DemonstrativePronounsGenerated ;
DemonstrativeAdverbRootsGenerated ;
DemonstrativePronounRootsGenerated ;

! The demonstrative pronoun/adverb system (tools/fst/generate_demonstratives.py
! -- see that script's own docstring for the full investigation) is an
! entire root+ending category, not an extension of an already-partially-
! wired mechanism: Demonstratives.csv's 65 rows give either a STANDALONE
! complete word (own Root entry point, e.g. "tamanna" = "this one",
! reachable from DemonstrativeAdverbsGenerated/DemonstrativePronounsGenerated)
! or a ROOT that takes a case ending from Endings_demonstrative.csv (a
! SEPARATE Root entry point, e.g. "taakku"+"ninga" = "taakkuninga",
! reachable from DemonstrativeAdverbRootsGenerated/
! DemonstrativePronounRootsGenerated) -- both forms come from the SAME CSV
! row, confirmed by reverse-engineering the tag shapes real gold ids use
! (MorphAnalGoldStandard_Hansard.kt has both "tamannali" =
! {tamanna:tamanna/pd-ml-s}{li:li/1q} and "taakkuninga" =
! {taakku:taakku/rpd-sc-p}{ninga:ninga/tpd-acc-p}, same underlying row
! backing each). No phonology at all: neither source CSV has an action
! column, so every entry is plain concatenation.
!
! Verified via histogram.py + a snapshot_correct.py diff: zero
! regressions, and the bulk generation's own breadth reached well beyond
! the handful of words individually tested. Two accepted false positives,
! both understood, not new bug classes: "taaksumunga" -- its OWN gold
! entry's canonical ("taangna") is the dictionary/morpheme form, unlike
! every other demonstrative gold word (which all use the CSV's "root"
! column as canonical, matching this generator's own choice; also the
! only gold string in this whole corpus with an odd duplicated-prefix
! formatting quirk) -- treated as a probable gold-data anomaly, not a
! reason to special-case the generator against every other word's
! pattern. "ukunani" -- an unrelated, not-yet-implemented verb root "uku"
! (+"nani"/tv-part-3s) accidentally spells the same string as the
! demonstrative root "uku"+"nani"/tpd-loc-p -- the same cross-lexical
! shadowing risk already documented and accepted throughout this file
! (e.g. nunalik/uqausiq/kiinaujaq), not specific to demonstratives.

! Noun root + terminal noun ending, straight concatenation, no
! phonological alternation: "akinga" = {aki:aki/1n}{nga:nga/tn-nom-s-4s}.

LEXICON Nouns
aki+1n:aki NounContinuations ;
arnaq+1n:arnaq NounContinuations ;
iglu+1n:iglu NounContinuations ;

! "illu" spelling variant of "iglu" (1n, canonical "iglu" per gold:
! "{illu:iglu/1n}") -- NOT a conditioned alternation despite looking
! like one at first (many gold "illu*" words involve a
! consonant-initial ending, which invited the wrong guess that this
! might be phonologically triggered): gold attests the BARE root itself
! both ways ("illu" alone, no ending at all) and lists
! "iglulirijikkut"/"illulirijikkut" (and two more "liri"-suffixed
! siblings) as separate entries for the IDENTICAL decomposition -- free
! spelling variation across every context, same "wire both, let the
! input string pick" treatment as missa/mitsa (miksa) and issiva/itsiva
! (iksiva) above.
iglu+1n:illu NounContinuations ;

! "qulluktuq" spelling variant of "kugluktuk" (1n, already bulk-
! generated from RootsSpalding.csv's own "variant" column) needs KGUARD
! protection (phonology.xfscript) -- its own internal "k" immediately
! precedes its own "t", which the blanket k->t rule silently corrupts
! into "qulluttuq" otherwise. Added here as a parallel, GUARDED entry
! (the plain bulk-generated one stays, just never actually reachable
! for this literal without the guard).
kugluktuk+1n:qullukKGUARDtuq NounContinuations ;

! "tulli" spelling variant of "tugli" (1n, canonical "tugli" per gold:
! "{tulli:tugli/1n}") -- same unexplained "gl"->"ll" alternation
! category as "iglu"->"illu"/"iglaq"->"illaq" above, confirmed via the
! real Java analyzer's own output before wiring ("tullia").
tugli+1n:tulli NounContinuations ;

! "qallunaa" spelling variant of "qaplunaaq" (1n, canonical "qaplunaaq"
! per gold: "{qallunaa:qaplunaaq/1n}") -- an unexplained root-internal
! alternation, same "iglu"->"illu" category, already flagged as a known
! gap further down in this file (NounEndings' own "inuk"/"titut"
! comment) but never actually wired until now. "qallunaat" needs it
! directly (root + "it"/tn-nom-p); confirmed via the real Java
! analyzer's own output before wiring.
qaplunaaq+1n:qallunaa NounContinuations ;

! "arragu" spelling variant of "arraagu"/1n (single vs double "a"),
! found the same way as "it"/tn-nom-p above (an already-correct gold
! sibling, "arraagumi", exists for the identical decomposition as the
! failing "arragumi").
arraagu+1n:arragu NounContinuations ;

! "nunattiaq" spelling variant of "nunatsiaq"/1n (ts->tt), found the
! same way: "nunatsiap" is already correct, "nunattiap" shares its
! exact decomposition.
nunatsiaq+1n:nunattiaq NounContinuations ;

! Three more root-internal spelling variants, found via the false-
! positive cluster analysis (a wrong SHORTER root was winning because
! the CSV's own canonical spelling didn't match gold's surface at all):
! "ullaaq" variant of "ublaaq"/1n ("morning", b->l -- gold: "ullaaq"
! bare and "ullaakkut"); "unikkaaq" variant of "unipkaaq"/1n ("story",
! p->k plus the resulting cluster doubling -- gold: "unikkaaq"/
! "unikkaat"/"unikkaangat"/"unikkaangit"); "unnusaq" variant of
! "unnuksaq"/1n ("afternoon", own "k" dropped -- gold: "unnusami").
ublaaq+1n:ullaaq NounContinuations ;
unipkaaq+1n:unikkaaq NounContinuations ;
unnuksaq+1n:unnusaq NounContinuations ;

! Eight more bare-root spelling variants, all found the same
! systematic way as the demonstrative-system sweep above (a script
! cross-referencing every gold word that's a SINGLE atomic root against
! every currently-wired spelling for that exact canonical+tag, rather
! than noticing mismatches one at a time): "iqaluttuuttiaq" variant of
! "iqaluktuutsiaq"/1n; "milian" 4th variant of "miliat"/1n (alongside
! the existing miliat/milliat/milijat) -- this ALSO resolves the
! previously-accepted "milianik"/"milianit" false-positive collisions
! documented elsewhere in this file, since gold's own canonical for
! bare "milian" is this SAME "miliat" root, not a coincidental
! unrelated homograph as first assumed; "namminiq" variant of
! "nangminiq"/1n; "natsilik" variant of "nattilik"/1n; "panniqtuuq"
! variant of "pangnirtuuq"/1n; "qauppat" variant of "qaukpat"/1n;
! "tausan" variant of "tausat"/1n (alongside the existing "tausa");
! "ulluq" variant of "ubluq"/1n.
iqaluktuutsiaq+1n:iqaluttuuttiaq NounContinuations ;
miliat+1n:milian NounContinuations ;
nangminiq+1n:namminiq NounContinuations ;
nattilik+1n:natsilik NounContinuations ;
pangnirtuuq+1n:panniqtuuq NounContinuations ;
qaukpat+1n:qauppat NounContinuations ;
tausat+1n:tausan NounContinuations ;
ubluq+1n:ulluq NounContinuations ;

! "kanannaq"/"uannaq" spelling variants of "kanangnaq"/1n ("the
! north-east") and "uangnaq"/1n ("the north-west") -- needed for
! "kanannangani"/"uannangani", both gold-attested as root+"ngani"/
! tn-loc-s-4s. Not the same as RootsSpalding.csv's own "variant" column
! for these two rows (kanangniq/uangniq -- a different alternation,
! unrelated), so hand-added here rather than read from the CSV: the
! root's own internal "ngn"->"nn" simplifies before "ngani" attaches
! ("kanangnaq"->"kanannaq"+SUPPR(own q)+"ngani" = "kanannangani"),
! same free-variation-by-evidence treatment as "iglu"/"illu" above,
! just for a root-internal cluster instead of the whole word.
kanangnaq+1n:kanannaq NounContinuations ;
uangnaq+1n:uannaq NounContinuations ;

! "minista" (loanword "minister") and "piliriaq" ("program; item") come
! from LoanWords.csv and UndecomposableCompositeWords.csv respectively --
! root CSVs that exist (core/.../dataCSV/) but that generate_roots.py's
! bulk pass doesn't cover.
minista+1n:minista NounContinuations ;
piliriaq+1n:piliriaq NounContinuations ;

! "gavama" ("government", LoanWords.csv) hand-added, same reasoning as
! "minista"/"piliriaq" above.
gavama+1n:gavama NounContinuations ;

! "tusaaji" ("interpreter", WordsRelatedToRoots.csv) hand-added -- a root
! CSV generate_roots.py's bulk pass doesn't cover.
tusaaji+1n:tusaaji NounContinuations ;

! "missa"/"mitsa" spelling variants of the bulk-generated "miksa" root
! (1n, canonical "miksa" per gold: "{missa:miksa/1n}"/"{mitsa:miksa/1n}")
! -- the bulk generator only emits the identity spelling for this root.
miksa+1n:missa NounContinuations ;
miksa+1n:mitsa NounContinuations ;

! "nunavut" ("Nunavut", 1n) -- a legitimate root generate_roots.py's bulk
! pass never covers: it lives in Locations.csv, a root-source CSV the
! bulk generator isn't extended to. Hand-added both the identity spelling
! ("nunavut", whose own trailing t assimilates to a following "m" for
! free via the general t->m rule below) and a t-deleted variant
! ("nunavu", the other gold-attested outcome for the same context --
! genuine free variation, same shape as usiq/naq/miik elsewhere in this
! file).
nunavut+1n:nunavut NounContinuations ;
nunavut+1n:nunavu NounContinuations ;

! Fan-out hubs so EVERY noun/verb root (hand-picked or bulk-generated) can
! reach every applicable suffix/ending class generically, not just the
! one lexicon the specific word that introduced it happened to need --
! e.g. every noun root should be able to take a noun-to-noun or
! noun-to-verb derivational suffix, not just one specific ending. Purely
! additive (new reachable paths, not new transformations), so it doesn't
! change what already-validated words do -- reverified by rerunning
! tools/fst/histogram.py after this change.

LEXICON NounContinuations
NounEndings ;
NnSuffixes ;
NvSuffixes ;
NnSuffixesGenerated ;
NvSuffixesGenerated ;
TnEndingsGenerated ;
! *Speculative variants (see suffixes-generated.lexc's own header for
! what that means): wired into the SAME hub as their non-speculative
! siblings so they're actually reachable, not a weaker/separate path.
NnSuffixesGeneratedSpeculative ;
NvSuffixesGeneratedSpeculative ;
TnEndingsGeneratedSpeculative ;
# ;

LEXICON VerbContinuations
VnSuffixes ;
VvSuffixes ;
TvEndings ;
VnSuffixesGenerated ;
VvSuffixesGenerated ;
TvEndingsGenerated ;
VnSuffixesGeneratedSpeculative ;
VvSuffixesGeneratedSpeculative ;
TvEndingsGeneratedSpeculative ;

LEXICON NounEndings

! "ngangnit"/tn-abl-s-4d (dual ablative, "his/her/their two X's"):
! "katimajingannit" is gold's only tn-abl-s-4d example, and its own
! surface span is "ngannit" -- identical to the already-implemented
! "ngannit"/tn-abl-s-4p (PLURAL) spelling, not the canonical "ngangnit"
! Endings_noun.csv's own V-form gives (no reduced candidate documented
! there at all). A real dual/plural spelling homograph, not a bug --
! same "wire the attested literal, let the input string pick" treatment
! as every other spelling variant this session, just this once the
! variant happens to coincide with a DIFFERENT tag's own spelling.
++ngangnit+tn-abl-s-4d:ngannit # ;

! "nga"/tn-nom-s-4s's own SECOND V-context candidate: Endings_noun.csv
! gives V-form "nga a" (2 space-separated candidates), the first
! ("nga", already wired) with a clean action2 ("-"), the second ("a")
! with action2 "s" -- not the same "preceding-stem-vowel-suppression"
! shape confirmed for nganit/tn-abl-s-4s's own "anit" candidate (that
! one paired action2="s" with action1="s" too; here action1 is "n"), so
! left uninvestigated for its general semantics -- "naasautaa"/
! "uqaalautaa" both need this literal ("a", already a plain reduced
! form in the CSV, not derived) directly, confirmed via the real Java
! analyzer's own output before wiring.
++nga+tn-nom-s-4s:a # ;

! Same "a" literal, q-context (SUPPR deletes a preceding q-final root's
! own trailing q): "tungilia" (root "tungiliq", q-final) needs it,
! confirmed via the real Java analyzer's own output before wiring.
++nga+tn-nom-s-4s:SUPPRa # ;

! "nganit"/tn-abl-s-4s's own SECOND q-context candidate: Endings_noun.csv
! gives q-form "nganit anit" (2 space-separated candidates), both
! action1 Suppression -- the bulk generator only ever wires the FIRST
! ("SUPPRnganit", already in endings-generated.lexc), since the second
! candidate's own action2 ("s") isn't a code generate_affixes.py
! understands yet (unlike "decap", the only action2 value currently
! handled). "aippaanit" needs this second candidate specifically:
! "aippaq"+SUPPR(deletes the q)+"anit" = "aippaanit", confirmed directly
! via hfst-lookup before wiring -- "anit" is already the CSV's own
! literal (not derived by a new rule), so just needs the same SUPPR
! marker action1 already calls for.
++nganit+tn-abl-s-4s:SUPPRanit # ;

! "k"/tn-nom-d (dual nominative): "ministaa"/"iksivautaa"/"ajjaqsijii"/
! etc. Endings_noun.csv's V-context action pair is VowelLengthening+
! Cancellation -- a genuinely NEW mechanism, not a marker-scoped rewrite
! of the PRECEDING stem (like NASAL/VOICE) but a COPY of whatever vowel
! immediately precedes, with the ending's own canonical "k" contributing
! NOTHING else to the surface at all ("minista"+"a"(doubled)="ministaa",
! not "minista"+"a"+"k"). New TNNOMD marker: duplicates a/i/u (whichever
! immediately precedes it), phonology.xfscript. t/k/q-context (Insertion
! "i" / Suppression+VowelLengthening) not attempted: every gold word in
! this cluster is vowel-final by the time "k" attaches.
++k+tn-nom-d:TNNOMD # ;

! "ptingni"/tn-loc-s-1d (dual locative): Endings_noun.csv flags this
! row's V-context as Neutral (no change), but that's misleading -- CSV
! V/t/k/q columns only ever describe what happens based on the PRECEDING
! stem, and every gold example (all vowel-final roots: arraagu/kinguni/
! nuna/sivuni) shows the SAME internal reduction regardless: "ptingni" ->
! "ttinni" (p assimilates to its own following t, same general p->t rule
! as "gapta" below; "ng"->"n" simplifies too). Unconditional on preceding
! context, so implemented as a plain literal surface text, same
! "canonical citation form differs from the always-used surface form"
! shape as "ralaaq" in NnSuffixes below -- no marker, no guessed trigger
! condition. Also needed a SUPPR-prefixed variant for when the
! immediately preceding morpheme has its own trailing consonant to shed
! (needed for "nunalittinni" via lik/1nn).
++ptingni+tn-loc-s-1d:ttinni # ;
++ptingni+tn-loc-s-1d:SUPPRttinni # ;

! The same "ptingni"->"ttinni" reduction (p->t, ng->n) applies to this
! ending's plural-1p siblings too (tn-loc-p-1p/tn-acc-p-1p/tn-dat-p-1p,
! needed by "uva"/1rpr, a bulk-generated Pronouns.csv "rpr"-type root --
! see generate_roots.py's own comment on load_pronouns_csv) --
! Endings_noun.csv's own literal text for those rows is the unprocessed
! "ptingni"/"ptingnik"/"ptingnut" (bulk-generated as-is in
! endings-generated.lexc, harmless but never matches any real gold
! surface), so the corrected spelling is hand-added here rather than
! guessing at a general rule from a single root family.
++ptingni+tn-loc-p-1p:ttinni # ;
++ptingnik+tn-acc-p-1p:ttinnik # ;
++ptingnut+tn-dat-p-1p:ttinnut # ;

! "ngita"/tn-gen-p-4s: clean single V-context candidate per
! Endings_noun.csv (Neutral, bare "ngita"). "gavamakkungita" (kkut/1nn,
! t-final) needed SUPPR rather than the general t->n rule: t->n would
! give "kkunngita" (double n, since ngita's own leading "ng" already
! supplies one) instead of gold's single-n "kkungita" -- SUPPR runs
! before the general t->n rule in the cascade (phonology.xfscript), so
! deleting kkut's own t outright avoids the conflict.
++ngita+tn-gen-p-4s:SUPPRngita # ;

! "ga"/tn-nom-s-1s ("my X"): Endings_noun.csv gives TWO real candidates
! here, not one: V-context "ga" (Neutral, plain) confirmed via
! "apiqqutiga" (root chain ends in vowel "i"); q-context "ra" (Fusion --
! mechanically identical to SUPPR, deletes the preceding q) confirmed via
! BOTH "apiqqusira" (usiq's own "qusiq" candidate, q kept) and
! "tungilira" (root "tungiliq", q-final) -- two independent roots
! agreeing on the same q-context form, not a guess. t/k-context
! (Insertion "i" / Suppression) not attempted: no gold word in this
! cluster needs them.
++ga+tn-nom-s-1s:ga # ;
++ga+tn-nom-s-1s:ga QParticles ;
++ga+tn-nom-s-1s:SUPPRra # ;

++nga+tn-nom-s-4s:nga # ;

! "it"/tn-nom-p: {arna:arnaq/1n}{it:it/tn-nom-p} = "arnait" and
! {iglu:iglu/1n}{it:it/tn-nom-p} = "igluit". Endings_noun.csv's "it" row
! has TWO actions per context (action1, action2): action1 is the familiar
! Suppression/Neutral; action2 is Selfdecapitation (Action.kt: strips the
! affix's OWN first letter, "it"->"t"), firing only when the stem left
! behind by action1 would end in two vowels, to avoid a 3-vowel run --
! forced into the open by "arraagutamaat" (see "tamaaq"/1nn's comment in
! NnSuffixes below). New DECAP marker: SUPPR still fires first (deletes
! a preceding q/k/t if present), then a rule deletes "it"'s own leading
! "i" specifically when the segment immediately before the marker is two
! vowels, then the marker itself is dropped -- verified in isolation (a
! toy "...aaqSUPPRDECAPit" string through analogous rules) before
! touching this entry. Correct for the V-context ("iglu", no deletion,
! and "iglu" itself never ends in two vowels so decap stays inert) and
! the q-context ("arnaq"/"arraagutamaaq") alike. NOT yet correct for a
! t-final root: this ending's own t-context action is Neutral, not
! Suppression, but the existing SUPPR rule generalizes deletion across
! q/k/t uniformly -- so a t-final root reaching this entry would still
! wrongly lose its final t. Deferred rather than guessed at: fix when a
! gold-standard word actually needs the t-context.
! Also has an UNCONDITIONAL "t"-only spelling, own leading "i" dropped
! regardless of how many vowels precede -- not the same thing as DECAP
! (which only strips it when exactly two vowels precede): gold attests
! "katimajiit" (the DECAP-inert full spelling, one vowel precedes,
! matching the documented behavior above) and "katimajit" (the
! reduced spelling) as separate entries for the IDENTICAL
! decomposition, so this is genuine free variation on top of the
! documented DECAP mechanism, not a replacement for it. Found by
! testing whether "combination mismatch" gold words sharing an
! "it"/tn-nom-p tail might be free-variant spellings rather than a
! deeper phonology gap -- confirmed for several at once
! ("piliriaksat"/"piqujaksat"/"uqausiksat", all ksaq/1nn+it chains;
! "pigiaqtitat", a jaq/1vn+it chain), not just "katimajit".
++it+tn-nom-p:SUPPRDECAPit # ;
++it+tn-nom-p:SUPPRt # ;

! "i"-only spelling (own trailing "t" dropped, "i" kept -- NOT the
! DECAP mechanism, which deletes the ending's OWN LEADING letter, and
! doesn't apply here since "ji"/1vn's own trailing "i" is only ONE
! vowel, not DECAP's required two): "titiraqtii"/"uqartii"/
! "maligaliuqtii" all need it directly after "ji"'s own "ti" spelling
! (j->t already automatic via the general rule). None of these three
! words are decomposable by the real Java analyzer either (confirmed
! via --pipeline) -- this project's own gold-evidence-driven
! methodology, no reference output to check against here.
++it+tn-nom-p:i # ;

! "Lever A": the id-conditional q-context pattern shared by mut/tn-dat-s,
! mik/tn-acc-s, mi/tn-loc-s, nit/tn-abl-p, ni/tn-loc-p, nik/tn-acc-p.
! Endings_noun.csv's q-form/q-action1/q-action2 for each of these endings
! carries TWO space-separated candidates:
!   candidate A: the ending's own text unchanged, action1 =
!     "if(id:juq/1vn|id:ksaq/1nn|id:jaq/3vn[|id:jaq/1vn],s,nas)" -- a
!     genuinely deterministic conditional (confirmed by reading
!     core/.../morph/r2l/MorphAnalyzerValidation.kt's
!     validate_conditionaldeletion_null/validate_conditionalnasalization_null
!     and MorphologicalAnalyzer_R2L.kt's checkValidityOfRoot: the source
!     analyzer defers this exact condition as a constraint checked against
!     whichever morpheme the real search actually finds immediately
!     preceding, NOT resolved by guessing -- so "the id of the immediately
!     preceding morpheme" is a real, checkable fact, not lexical
!     ambiguity): IF that preceding morpheme's id is one of {juq/1vn,
!     ksaq/1nn, jaq/3vn} (jaq/1vn also listed for mut specifically) THEN
!     Suppression (delete the preceding q) ELSE Nasalization (q->r,
!     reusing NASAL).
!   candidate B: the ending's own text unchanged, action1=Neutral,
!     action2=Suppression -- a SECOND, unconditioned candidate that also
!     deletes a preceding q, independent of the conditional above.
! Real gold words confirm BOTH candidates are independently attested, not
! redundant: "maligarmut"/"maligarmi"/"maligarmik"/"maligarnit" (root
! "malik"+"gaq"/1vn, NOT a trigger id -> candidate A's ELSE branch,
! Nasalization: q->r) versus "nutaamut"/"nutaami"/"nutaamik"/"nutaanit"/
! "nutaanik" (root "nutaaq" directly, also not a trigger id, but here
! candidate B applies: plain Suppression, q simply deleted, no "r") --
! same root class (a bare noun root), genuinely two different outcomes,
! not something guessable from the CSV row alone. Both wired as separate
! lexc entries (NASAL-marked = candidate A's else-branch, SUPPR-marked =
! candidate B) reachable from the generic NounEndings hub (any q-final
! stem), exactly mirroring how the source analyzer's own real
! backtracking search offers both and lets whichever one matches the
! actual word win -- hfst-lookup does the same thing here, returning
! multiple analyses, same accepted pattern as every other multi-candidate
! lexc entry in this file (e.g. "vugut"'s V vs t/k branches).
!
! Candidate A's THEN branch (Suppression, triggered specifically by a
! preceding juq/1vn, ksaq/1nn, or jaq/1vn -- jaq/3vn not implemented) is
! wired separately, in a dedicated "NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix"
! lexicon below, reached from juq/1vn's own and ksaq/1nn's own entries
! (VnSuffixes/NnSuffixes below). Confirmed against "maannaujumi" (juq
! trigger, mi), "angijumik" (juq trigger, mik), "aviktursimajuni" (juq
! trigger, ni), "maligaksanit" (ksaq trigger, nit) -- all four, the
! trigger morpheme's own trailing q is deleted (Suppression) rather than
! nasalized. mut's own trigger branch and jaq/1vn's own wire into this
! lexicon are NOT added: no gold word in the current lexicon's reach
! needs them yet -- deferred rather than wired speculatively. ni's own
! default (non-trigger) NASAL/SUPPR branches are likewise NOT wired: no
! gold word attests either one for "ni" specifically with a root already
! in this lexicon.
!
! Known extra false-positive risk from this default-branch SUPPR-marked
! entries specifically (distinct from candidate A's NASAL entries, which
! only ever touch a genuine q): SUPPR was always defined to delete
! whatever consonant precedes it out of q/k/t INDISCRIMINATELY, reachable
! now from the generic NounEndings hub, it fires for a T-FINAL root
! reaching one of these new entries too, not just the Q-final case
! candidate B's CSV row was actually describing (confirmed:
! "milianik"/"milianit" -- unrelated gold words with root "milian" --
! now also match via bulk-generated root "miliat" + SUPPRnik/SUPPRnit,
! "miliat"'s own final t deleted the same way a q would be). Same
! accepted/canary-tracked risk category as every other plain-unmarked or
! generically-scoped entry in this file, not a new kind of bug --
! full_corpus_check.py's correct-not-present count is the ongoing signal.
!
! "mut"/tn-dat-s: "arraagumut" = {arraagu:arraagu/1n}{mut:mut/tn-dat-s}
! (V-context, plain, single candidate). The t-context is NOT implemented:
! it has three candidate forms and no algorithmic disambiguator. The
! q-context is Lever A itself, described above. A consonant-final root
! reaching the plain V-context entry concatenates "mut" unchanged, which
! is likely WRONG for a t-final stem (not modeling the real t-context
! behavior) -- a known, accepted risk, canary-checked by rerunning
! tools/fst/full_corpus_check.py (its "correct-not-present" count is
! exactly the signal for this).
++mut+tn-dat-s:mut # ;
++mut+tn-dat-s:NASALmut # ;
++mut+tn-dat-s:SUPPRmut # ;

! "mit"/tn-abl-s: same Lever A shape as mut/nik/etc's default branch
! (plain/NASAL/SUPPR wired in parallel; its own q-form is the same
! id-conditional pattern as those, and "paaq"/1nn -- see
! "kingulliqpaamit"/"sivulliqpaamit" -- isn't one of the trigger ids, so
! it falls to the default branch).
++mit+tn-abl-s:mit # ;
++mit+tn-abl-s:NASALmit # ;
++mit+tn-abl-s:SUPPRmit # ;

! "nik"/tn-acc-p: "arraagunik" = {arraagu:arraagu/1n}{nik:nik/tn-acc-p}
! -- V-context only (V-form=nik/Neutral, single candidate). The
! t/k-context is deferred the same way as mut's t-context (k-context is
! the Lever A id-conditional pattern); same accepted plain-unmarked-entry
! risk as "mut", canary-checked by full_corpus_check.py's
! "correct-not-present" count.
++nik+tn-acc-p:nik # ;
++nik+tn-acc-p:NASALnik # ;
++nik+tn-acc-p:SUPPRnik # ;

! "ngit"/tn-nom-p-4s: "akingit" = {aki:aki/1n}{ngit:ngit/tn-nom-p-4s}
! (V-context, plain) and "atingit" = {ati:atiq/1n}{ngit:ngit/tn-nom-p-4s}
! (q-context, root's final q deleted). V-form=ngit/Neutral,
! k/q-form=ngit/Suppression -- all single candidate, genuine rule, reuses
! SUPPR unchanged. t-context has two candidates (Insertion "i" vs
! Suppression, no algorithmic disambiguator) -- deferred, same policy as
! every such case.
++ngit+tn-nom-p-4s:SUPPRngit # ;
++ngit+tn-nom-p-4s:SUPPRngit QParticles ;

! Also an unconditional "ngi"-only spelling (own trailing "t"
! dropped), found via already-correct gold siblings ("asingit"/
! "ilangit" alongside the failing "asingi"/"ilangi", same
! decomposition each) -- same "extra truncated free variant"
! shape as "it"/tn-nom-p's own "t"-only candidate above.
++ngit+tn-nom-p-4s:SUPPRngi # ;

! "ni"/tn-loc-p: "amisuni" = {amisu:amisu/1n}{ni:ni/tn-loc-p}. V-only
! (V-form=ni/Neutral); t/k/q all ambiguous or id-conditional, deferred.
++ni+tn-loc-p:ni # ;

! Also a SUPPR-prefixed default-branch candidate (Lever A's own
! q-context pattern, described above, extended to "ni" specifically):
! "avittuqsimajuni" needs "juq"/1vn's own trailing q deleted before
! "ni" attaches -- not attested for "ni" before now (see the Lever A
! comment above, which explicitly deferred this), confirmed by this
! real example rather than wired speculatively.
++ni+tn-loc-p:SUPPRni # ;

! "mik"/tn-acc-s: "ministamik" = {minista:minista/1n}{mik:mik/tn-acc-s}.
! V-only, same deferral pattern as "mut"/"nik". (Not "illumik" =
! {illu:iglu/1n}{mik:mik/tn-acc-s}, despite "iglu" already being a
! lexicon root: it surfaces here as "illu" -- a g->l alternation not seen
! when the same root attaches to "it"/tn-nom-p ("igluit", unchanged) --
! not understood yet, avoided rather than guessed at.)
++mik+tn-acc-s:mik # ;
++mik+tn-acc-s:NASALmik # ;
++mik+tn-acc-s:SUPPRmik # ;

! "nginnut"/tn-dat-p-4s: "akinginnut" =
! {aki:aki/1n}{nginnut:nginnut/tn-dat-p-4s}. V+k+q (all single candidate,
! k/q both Suppression, reuses SUPPR); t-context ambiguous, deferred.
! Note: Endings_noun.csv has TWO "nginnut" rows (perPoss=4, numbPoss=s vs
! numbPoss=p) -- used the numbPoss=s one (matches the gold id
! "tn-dat-p-4s" exactly); the numbPoss=p row is a different id, not
! implemented.
++nginnut+tn-dat-p-4s:SUPPRnginnut # ;
++nginnut+tn-dat-p-4s:SUPPRnginnut QParticles ;

! "nginnik"/tn-acc-p-4s: same shape as nginnut/nginnit/nginni (V-context
! Neutral, reuses SUPPR for the k/q-context Suppression rows, none of
! which are gold-attested here).
++nginnik+tn-acc-p-4s:SUPPRnginnik # ;
++nginnik+tn-acc-p-4s:SUPPRnginnik QParticles ;

! "nut"/tn-dat-p: same shared NounEndings hub deliberately serves "it"
! (reached from bare noun roots via NounContinuations) and "nut" (reached
! from NnSuffixes-derived stems like "kkut"): "it" and "nut" should
! always be the same reachable set, since ANY noun-like stem can take ANY
! tn-ending -- e.g. "tuinnaq"/1nn (NnSuffixes) needs to reach "it" too.
! Gained the same default-branch NASAL/SUPPR pair as Lever A's other
! endings above: "surusirnut" (root "surusiq", Nasalization: q->r) versus
! "nutaanut"/"ukiunut" (roots "nutaaq"/"ukiuq", Suppression: q simply
! deleted) -- same root-dependent split, both real. nut's own TRIGGER
! branch (Suppression when preceded specifically by juq/1vn/ksaq/1nn/
! jaq/3vn) is wired in NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix below, confirmed
! via "ajjigiinngittunut".
++nut+tn-dat-p:nut # ;
++nut+tn-dat-p:NASALnut # ;
++nut+tn-dat-p:SUPPRnut # ;

! Also an unconditional "nu"-only spelling (own trailing "t" dropped),
! found via already-correct gold siblings ("inunnut"/"inungnut"
! alongside the failing "inunnu"; "nunalingnut"/"nunalinnut" alongside
! the failing "nunalinnu"). Plain, NOT SUPPR-prefixed: the doubled "n"
! these words need ("inuk"+"nu" -> "inunnu") comes from a NEW general
! k->n assimilation rule (phonology.xfscript, same total-regressive-
! assimilation family as t->n/k->t/p->t/t->m/k->m/m->n) firing on the
! PRECEDING root's own final k -- SUPPR would delete that k outright
! before the assimilation rule ever got a chance, giving the wrong
! single-n "inunu" instead. The same new rule also resolves
! "inunnut"/"nunalinnut" for free via the EXISTING plain "nut"
! candidate above, no lexc change needed for those two.
++nut+tn-dat-p:nu # ;

! "inuusilirijikkunullu" needs "nut"/tn-dat-p to ALSO reach QParticles
! (lu/1q's own enclitic can follow a fully-inflected noun, same
! established pattern as "ga"/tn-nom-s-1s etc above).
++nut+tn-dat-p:nut QParticles ;
++nut+tn-dat-p:NASALnut QParticles ;
++nut+tn-dat-p:SUPPRnut QParticles ;
++nut+tn-dat-p:nu QParticles ;

! "titut"/tn-sim-p is a K-CONTEXT (not q) single-candidate Neutral row --
! same literal "titut" text as V-context, so needs no separate marker,
! one plain entry covers both. Target word is "inuttitut" (root "inuk",
! k-final), NOT the more obvious "inuktitut": the general k->t rule below
! (for "quviattunga") correctly assimilates "inuk"+"titut" -> "inuttitut"
! -- confirmed by testing the generator direction directly. "inuktitut"
! (no assimilation) is gold-attested too but almost certainly the
! lexicalized proper-noun spelling of the language name itself, not a
! compositional form; left unimplemented rather than fighting an
! already-correct general rule for one irregular spelling. Its own
! q-context is the same Lever A trigger-conditional shape, but NOT
! implemented: the one gold word that would exercise it
! ("qallunaatitut") has an unrelated, unexplained root-internal
! alternation (qaplunaaq -> qallunaa, same category as iglu->illu), so
! there's no clean example to verify against.
!
! "mit"/tn-abl-s was investigated with the same V+trigger+default shape
! as "mut" and initially left unimplemented: every gold word that would
! exercise its q-context chained through an already-unimplemented
! dependency (luaq/1vv) or an unrelated root alternation, and no
! V-context example existed either -- since implemented above once
! "kingulliqpaamit"/"sivulliqpaamit" (paaq/1nn) provided a clean example.
! "tut"/tn-sim-s remains unattested anywhere in the 985-word gold
! standard, not worth implementing blind.
++titut+tn-sim-p:titut # ;

! "inuktitut" (k preserved, NOT assimilated) is ALSO gold-attested
! alongside "inuttitut" above -- previously left unimplemented on the
! assumption it was purely the lexicalized proper-noun spelling of the
! language name, not reachable without "fighting" the general k->t
! rule. Now that KGUARD exists (built for "qulluktuq"'s own root-
! internal k->t self-corruption), the same trick generalizes to an
! inter-morpheme boundary: a KGUARD-prefixed candidate here blocks the
! rule for JUST this parallel path, while the plain "titut" candidate
! above still assimilates normally for whatever other roots need it --
! not decomposable by the real Java analyzer either (confirmed via
! --pipeline).
++titut+tn-sim-p:KGUARDtitut # ;

! "mi"/tn-loc-s: "arraagumi" = {arraagu:arraagu/1n}{mi:mi/tn-loc-s} --
! V-context only (V-form=mi/Neutral, single candidate). t/k/q-contexts
! NOT implemented: t-context has two candidates (Assimilation/Insertion,
! no algorithmic disambiguator); k-context's action is the Lever A
! id-conditional pattern. Same accepted plain-unmarked-entry risk as
! "mut"/"nik", canary-checked by full_corpus_check.py's
! "correct-not-present" count.
++mi+tn-loc-s:mi # ;
++mi+tn-loc-s:NASALmi # ;
++mi+tn-loc-s:SUPPRmi # ;

! "nit"/tn-abl-p: "arraagunit" = {arraagu:arraagu/1n}{nit:nit/tn-abl-p}
! -- V-context only (V-form=nit/Neutral, single candidate). t-context has
! two candidates (Assimilation/Insertion, no disambiguator); q-context is
! Lever A, described above.
++nit+tn-abl-p:nit # ;
++nit+tn-abl-p:NASALnit # ;
++nit+tn-abl-p:SUPPRnit # ;

! "up"/tn-gen-s: "arraaguup" = {arraagu:arraagu/1n}{up:up/tn-gen-s}
! (V-context, plain concatenation). Same action1+action2 shape as
! "it"/tn-nom-p: V/k/q-form all carry Selfdecapitation as action2, which
! only fires when the stem left behind by action1 would end in two
! vowels -- not the case for "arraagu" (single-vowel-final), so not
! modeled here, same deliberate deferral as "it". k/q-context reuses
! SUPPR unchanged (Suppression, same mechanism as "it"/"liri"/"gaq"/
! "lik"/"ngit") -- mechanically identical and low-risk to extend even
! without its own gold-standard-attested k/q example handy, verified
! instead by the standard negative-form-rejected + full-corpus-
! regression checks. t-context has two candidates (Suppression/
! Insertion), deferred as usual.
++up+tn-gen-s:SUPPRup # ;

! Two more free-variant spellings, found the same way as "it"/
! tn-nom-p's own "t"-only candidate above (checking whether an
! already-correct gold "sibling" exists with one extra/fewer letter):
! "u"-only (own trailing "p" dropped -- gold attests both
! "ministaup" and "ministau" for the identical decomposition) and
! "p"-only (own leading "u" dropped, merging with a preceding vowel --
! gold attests both "iksivautaup" and "iksivautap"). This was ALSO an
! already-documented gap ("a bare 'p'-only candidate for up/tn-gen-s
! (blocks 'iksivautap')", noted under "ut"/1vn's own comment above)
! finally closed with a real example in hand.
++up+tn-gen-s:SUPPRu # ;
++up+tn-gen-s:SUPPRp # ;

! Three more V-context (or V+k/q) noun endings:
!   - "tigut"/tn-via-p ("via" case): "tusaajitigut" =
!     {tusaaji:tusaaji/1n}{tigut:tigut/tn-via-p}. V+k (both Neutral,
!     plain, no marker); t-context needs its own Insertion("i") marker
!     (not built, unused by this word since "tusaaji" is vowel-final);
!     q-context is id-conditional, deferred as usual.
!   - "nginnit"/tn-abl-p-4s: "asinginnit" =
!     {asi:asi/1n}{nginnit:nginnit/tn-abl-p-4s}. V+k+q (k/q both
!     Suppression, reuses SUPPR); t-context ambiguous, deferred.
!   - "nginni"/tn-loc-p-4s: "asinginni" =
!     {asi:asi/1n}{nginni:nginni/tn-loc-p-4s}. Same shape as "nginnit"
!     above (V+k+q via SUPPR, t deferred).
++tigut+tn-via-p:tigut # ;
++tigut+tn-via-p:tigut NounContinuations ;

! Also an unconditional "tigu"-only spelling (own trailing "t"
! dropped), found via an already-correct gold sibling
! ("tusaajitigut" alongside the failing "tusaajitigu"/
! "tusaajititigu", identical decomposition -- the latter also needs
! "ji"/1vn's own "titigu" spelling investigated separately, not
! attempted here).
++tigut+tn-via-p:tigu # ;

++nginnit+tn-abl-p-4s:SUPPRnginnit # ;
++nginnit+tn-abl-p-4s:SUPPRnginnit QParticles ;
++nginni+tn-loc-p-4s:SUPPRnginni # ;

! "ngat"/tn-nom-s-4p: "ilangat" = {ila:ila/1n}{ngat:ngat/tn-nom-s-4p} --
! V+k+q (k/q both Suppression, reuses SUPPR); t-context ambiguous (2
! candidates), deferred.
++ngat+tn-nom-s-4p:SUPPRngat # ;

! "ngagut"/tn-via-s-4s: Endings_noun.csv's row gives TWO V-context
! candidates in every column: full "ngagut" and reduced "agut" (missing
! its own leading "ng"). Checked every gold-attested root first (all
! vowel-final: asi/ila/ilu/kinguni/sivuni/tunga): NOT a phonological
! split by which vowel precedes -- "ila" (final a) needs the FULL form
! ("ilangagut") while "tunga" (also final a) needs the REDUCED form
! ("tungaagut") -- genuinely root-specific, not guessable from the CSV.
! Real gold words attest BOTH outcomes for different roots, so both are
! wired as parallel candidates rather than picked/abandoned -- matches
! how the source analyzer's own backtracking search would explore both.
! All 6 gold roots are vowel-final, so t/k/q-context are not
! gold-attested here and not attempted.
++ngagut+tn-via-s-4s:ngagut # ;
++ngagut+tn-via-s-4s:agut # ;

! "ngani"/tn-loc-s-4s: same shape as tn-via-s-4s just above (two
! candidates, different strings, wired in parallel exactly like
! ngagut/agut). Confirmed genuinely root-specific, not phonologically
! conditioned: "sivuni" (root, ends in "i") takes BOTH forms in separate
! gold words ("sivuniani" short, "sivuningani" full) -- proof this is
! real free variation, not something a vowel-class rule could predict
! either way. Also needed SUPPR-prefixed variants of both candidates for
! q-final roots ("qitiq" -> "qitingani", root's own trailing q deleted)
! -- same "V-context-only assumption breaks on a q-final root" trap seen
! throughout this file. Two gold words ("kanannangani"/"uannangani") NOT
! reached: their roots ("kanangnaq"/"uangnaq") undergo their OWN internal
! "ngn"->"nn" simplification before "ngani" attaches -- a genuine
! root-internal alternation, not ngani's problem, and only 2 words share
! it, not enough evidence to guess a general rule from.
++ngani+tn-loc-s-4s:ngani # ;
++ngani+tn-loc-s-4s:ani # ;
++ngani+tn-loc-s-4s:SUPPRngani # ;
++ngani+tn-loc-s-4s:SUPPRani # ;

! "nganut"/tn-dat-s-4s: sibling of "ngani" just above, identical shape
! and identical treatment, same free-variation confirmation ("miksa"
! root attested with BOTH "missaanut"/"mitsaanut" alternate root
! spellings, both taking the reduced "anut" form).
++nganut+tn-dat-s-4s:nganut # ;
++nganut+tn-dat-s-4s:anut # ;
++nganut+tn-dat-s-4s:SUPPRnganut # ;
++nganut+tn-dat-s-4s:SUPPRanut # ;

! "nganik"/tn-acc-s-4s: sibling of nganut/ngani above, same shape and
! same free-variation confirmation technique -- both target words attest
! the reduced "anik".
++nganik+tn-acc-s-4s:nganik # ;
++nganik+tn-acc-s-4s:anik # ;
++nganik+tn-acc-s-4s:SUPPRnganik # ;
++nganik+tn-acc-s-4s:SUPPRanik # ;

! "amittuq" = {amit:amit/1v}{tuq:juq/1vn} -- verb root + derivational
! (verb-to-noun) suffix whose canonical form "juq" surfaces as "tuq"
! after a t/k/q-final stem (rule in phonology.xfscript).

LEXICON Verbs
amit+1v:amit VerbContinuations ;
aanniaq+1v:aanniaq VerbContinuations ;
angi+1v:angi VerbContinuations ;

! "illaq" spelling variant of "iglaq" (1v, canonical "iglaq" per gold:
! "{illaq:iglaq/1v}") -- same unexplained root-internal "gl"->"ll"
! alternation category as "iglu"->"illu" above, confirmed via the real
! Java analyzer's own output before wiring ("illaqtut").
iglaq+1v:illaq VerbContinuations ;

! "aglat" spelling variant of "allak" (1v, canonical "allak" per gold:
! "{aglat:allak/1v}") -- an unexplained root-internal alternation
! (l->g, k->t), same free-variant-spelling category as "iglu"->"illu"
! above, just a different consonant pair. Confirmed via gold
! ("aglattiu"); not decomposable by the real Java analyzer either
! (confirmed via --pipeline).
allak+1v:aglat VerbContinuations ;

! "ilinniaq" ("to learn; to study") comes from CommonCompositeWords.csv --
! a root CSV that exists but that generate_roots.py's bulk pass doesn't
! cover. Hand-added, same reasoning as "minista"/"piliriaq" in Nouns
! above.
ilinniaq+1v:ilinniaq VerbContinuations ;

! "akiraq" ("to oppose; to retaliate", UndecomposableCompositeWords.csv)
! hand-added, same reasoning as "piliriaq"/"ilinniaq" above.
akiraq+1v:akiraq VerbContinuations ;

! "qaujima" ("to know") and "iqqanaijaq" ("to work") are from
! CommonCompositeWords.csv but excluded from generate_roots.py's bulk
! pass: "qaujima" has an empty "nb" column (the bulk generator's own
! required field), and "iqqanaijaq" has a populated "combination" column
! (the shadowing-risk filter). Both filters are doing their job correctly
! in general, but here they're overcautious: "qaujima"'s recorded
! decomposition is "qauji"+ a not-yet-implemented "ma"/1vv,
! "iqqanaijaq"'s is a chain through three more not-yet-implemented
! suffixes -- neither is actually reachable any other way in this
! lexicon, so there's no real shadowing risk, just a lost word.
! Hand-added rather than loosening the bulk filters for one row each.
qaujima+1v:qaujima VerbContinuations ;

! "apiri" ("to ask s.o. a question"): CommonCompositeWords.csv records
! this as a spelling variant of "apiq" (its own "combination" column just
! names "apiq", not a real multi-morpheme decomposition) -- same
! "shadowing-risk filter overcautious for this one row" shape as
! qaujima/iqqanaijaq above, hand-added rather than loosening the filter.
! Needed for "apirijumajara".
apiri+1v:apiri VerbContinuations ;
aulat+1v:aulat VerbContinuations ;
iqqanaijaq+1v:iqqanaijaq VerbContinuations ;

! "taimait" (1v, "to be like that"): WordsRelatedToRoots.csv records its
! own "combination" column as "taima/1a+it/3nv" -- but the gold
! standard's own decomposition of "taimaimmat"
! ({taimaim:taimait/1v}{mat:mat/tv-caus-4s}) treats "taimait" as its own
! atomic 1v root, NOT as taima+it (and "it"/3nv is a whole unimplemented
! ending category). Same "filter is overcautious for this one row" shape
! as qaujima/iqqanaijaq above -- hand-added rather than building the
! it/3nv ending just to reach the same surface string a different way.
taimait+1v:taimait VerbContinuations ;

! "issiva"/"itsiva" spelling variants of the bulk-generated "iksiva" root
! (1v, canonical "iksiva" per gold: "{issiva:iksiva/1v}"/
! "{itsiva:iksiva/1v}") -- generate_roots.py's bulk pass only ever emits
! the identity spelling (iksiva+1v:iksiva), so these dialectal surface
! variants need hand-adding the same way as "taimait" above, rather than
! looping the generator in over one CSV row's worth of extra spellings it
! was never designed to emit.
iksiva+1v:issiva VerbContinuations ;
iksiva+1v:itsiva VerbContinuations ;

! "niqsu"/"nirtu"/"niqtu" spelling variants of the bulk-generated
! "niqtuq" root (1v, canonical "niqtuq" per gold: "{niqsu:niqtuq/1v}"/
! "{nirtu:niqtuq/1v}"/"{niqtu:niqtuq/1v}" -- the last is the SAME letters
! as the canonical minus its own trailing q, easy to mistake for the
! bulk-generated identity entry, but it isn't -- the generated entry
! keeps the q) -- same "generator only emits the identity spelling" gap
! as taimait/issiva/itsiva/missa/mitsa.
niqtuq+1v:niqsu VerbContinuations ;
niqtuq+1v:nirtu VerbContinuations ;
niqtuq+1v:niqtu VerbContinuations ;

! "naammap" spelling variant of the bulk-generated "naamak" root (1v,
! canonical "naamak" per gold: "{naammap:naamak/1v}") -- an "m"-
! gemination + k->p change specific to this root before a following
! p-initial ending ("puq"/tv-dec-3s), not something the general v->p/k->p
! PMARK mechanism produces (same "generator only emits the identity
! spelling" gap as the others above, but the actual alternation here is
! root-internal and unexplained beyond this one attested word --
! hand-spelled rather than guessed as a general rule).
naamak+1v:naammap VerbContinuations ;

! "avit" spelling variant of "avik"/1v (k->t), found via an
! already-correct gold sibling ("avittuqsimajuni" alongside the
! failing "aviktursimajuni", identical decomposition).
avik+1v:avit VerbContinuations ;

! "mappiq" spelling variant of "makpiq"/1v (kp->pp, the same cluster
! simplification already seen for "qaukpat"->"qauppat"): "makpigaq" is
! already correct, "mappigaq" shares its exact decomposition.
makpiq+1v:mappiq VerbContinuations ;

! "aulat" ("to direct/govern s.t."): WordsRelatedToRoots.csv records this
! as "aula/1v+t/1vv", a compositional decomposition filtered out by
! generate_roots.py's shadowing-risk filter -- same "gold treats it as
! opaque, filter overcautious for this one row" shape as
! taimait/qaujima/apiri above. Needed for "aulattijiit"/
! "aulattinirmut" (si/1vv's t-context "ti" family).

! "aanniaqtulirijikkunnut" =
! {aanniaq:aanniaq/1v}{tu:juq/1vn}{liri:liri/1nv}{ji:ji/1vn}{kkun:kkut/1nn}
! {nut:nut/tn-dat-p} -- verb root, then vn -> nv -> vn -> nn -> tn, six
! morphemes. VnSuffixes/NvSuffixes are written as genuinely reusable
! continuation classes (not one-off per-word lexicons) so this word cycles
! back through the *same* VnSuffixes lexicon for both "juq" and "ji" --
! that's the actual mechanism this word exists to prove (per the plan:
! "Proves the continuation-class graph handles realistic derivational
! depth, not just a single suffix"), not just six more literal entries.
!
! Two distinct phonological phenomena here (see phonology.xfscript for the
! rules themselves), confirmed against the source Kotlin analyzer before
! writing either:
!   - "juq"+"liri": "juq"'s own j->t rule fires first (root "aanniaq" is
!     q-final), THEN the derived "tuq"'s final "q" is deleted specifically
!     because "liri" is one of the suffixes whose own q-context CSV row
!     (Suffixes.csv) carries a Suppression action on what precedes it -- a
!     property of this specific suffix, not a universal "q before l" sound
!     change. Modeled with an invisible SUPPR marker (below) rather than a
!     blanket context rule, so it doesn't accidentally delete every future
!     q-before-l sequence this lexicon might grow to include. (Named
!     SUPPR, not QDEL: the exact same Action.Suppression mechanism was
!     also found deleting a *different* final consonant -- "ilaak"'s k
!     before "qai" -- so this marker was generalized to "delete whatever
!     consonant precedes me", not q-specific.)
!   - "kkut"+"nut": "kkut"'s final "t" assimilates to "n" because "nut"
!     begins with "n" -- confirmed as a genuinely general, systematic
!     mechanism (Action.Assimilation, the same action code recurring in
!     hundreds of CSV rows across Suffixes.csv/Endings_noun.csv/
!     Endings_verb.csv), so this one *is* a direct, marker-free context
!     rule -- t immediately before n. Scoped narrowly to that one segment
!     pair for now (not the fully general "assimilates to whatever
!     consonant follows" rule the CSV data implies) since t-before-n is the
!     only instance any validated word exercises so far.
!   - The word's doubled "nn" (...kkunnut) is *not* a third phenomenon: it
!     falls out for free from the assimilation above plus plain
!     concatenation with "nut"'s already-lexical initial "n" -- no separate
!     rule or lexc entry needed for it.

LEXICON VnSuffixes
++juq+1vn:juq # ;

! "maannauju" = {maanna:maanna/1a}{u:u/1nv}{ju:juq/1vn} -- gold attests
! juq/1vn's own trailing q dropped at the bare terminal (no ending
! follows), a free spelling variant of the plain "juq" terminal above.
++juq+1vn:ju # ;

! "ju" (above) had only ever been tested at the bare terminal, the same
! "only tested one way" gap this project keeps re-finding -- missing its
! own continuation meant "qaujimajuinnaugatta" (needs "ju" to reach
! innaq/1nn in NnSuffixes) couldn't be found at all, confirmed via the
! real Java analyzer's own output before wiring.
++juq+1vn:ju NounContinuations ;
++juq+1vn:juq NounContinuations ;
++juq+1vn:juq AfterJuqTriggerSuffix ;

! "naammasaqtuit"/"naammasaqtut" need juq/1vn's own "tuq" spelling with
! ITS trailing q ALSO dropped, unlike the j->t conversion the general
! phonology.xfscript rule already produces automatically -- a SEPARATE,
! unconditional literal (not the same mechanism as "ju" above, which is
! V-context-only), confirmed via the real Java analyzer's own output
! (--pipeline) before wiring. ("qanuittuni"/"qanuittunik" superficially
! look like they'd need this too, but gold's chain for those actually
! needs the still-unimplemented "it"/3nv ending before juq -- this
! literal doesn't reach them, don't assume it does.)
++juq+1vn:tu # ;
++juq+1vn:tu NounContinuations ;

! "makkuktunut" (root "makkuk", k-final) needs "tu" with its own k
! preserved, NOT assimilated to "makkuttunut" -- same KGUARD trick as
! titut/tn-sim-p's own "inuktitut" candidate above (a parallel guarded
! path alongside the plain one, general rule still fires normally for
! whatever roots actually need it). Not decomposable by the real Java
! analyzer either (confirmed via --pipeline).
++juq+1vn:KGUARDtu # ;
++juq+1vn:KGUARDtu NounContinuations ;

! "ilinniartulirijiit" needs juq/1vn's "tu" candidate reaching a q-final
! root ("ilinniaq") with the root's own trailing q converted to r --
! same VOICE marker vik/3vn's own q-context candidate already uses
! (Endings_noun.csv's own comment on that entry documents "ilinniaq"'s
! q->r conversion directly), just not previously wired for juq/1vn's
! reduced spelling specifically.
++juq+1vn:VOICEtu NounContinuations ;

! "miik"/1vn (exclamation "Oh, how...!"): Suffixes.csv lists three
! literal spellings (miik/mii/mi) crossed with Nasalization vs
! Suppression actions in q-context -- but gold shows neither action
! cleanly: "nakuqmi"/"nakuqmii" keep the preceding root's q UNCHANGED
! (matching neither Suppression-deletes-it nor Nasalization-converts-it),
! while "nakurmii"/"nakurmiik" (same root "nakuq") DO show Nasalization
! (q->r). Same "wire plain and NASAL-marked variants in parallel, let
! gold's own spelling pick the path" strategy as usiq/1vn's SUPPR/VOICE
! split below -- all 3 spellings wired both plain and NASAL-prefixed (6
! entries total). "qujannami"/"qujannamik" (a 4th spelling, "mik", plus
! "naq"/1vv's own "nna" spelling and a "quja" root) not attempted: more
! unexplained variation than 2 words can justify guessing a rule from.
++miik+1vn:mi # ;
++miik+1vn:mii # ;
++miik+1vn:miik # ;
++miik+1vn:NASALmi # ;
++miik+1vn:NASALmii # ;
++miik+1vn:NASALmiik # ;

! "juq" also reaches a THIRD continuation, straight into a noun ending:
! "ajjigiinngittunik" needs it (juq -> nik/tn-acc-p) -- juq (verb-to-noun)
! had otherwise only ever continued to "#" or into another nv-suffix,
! never directly to a noun ending. Routed to a dedicated
! "NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix" lexicon below (rather than the shared
! "NounEndings", where "nik" ALSO independently lives, for the general
! case): several endings' own CSV rows delete a preceding q specifically
! when the id of what precedes them is juq/1vn (or ksaq/1nn, jaq/3vn/1vn
! -- a genuinely id-conditional context, "Lever A", see NounEndings
! above). Scoping it to a dedicated lexicon means this q-deletion stays
! specific to "reached right after one of these specific trigger
! suffixes" -- it doesn't leak into the general NounEndings case, whose
! own q-context uses a DIFFERENT mechanism (Nasalization by default).
++juq+1vn:juq NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix ;

++ji+1vn:ji NounContinuations ;
++ji+1vn:ji # ;

! "uqartii" needs the preceding root's own trailing q converted to r
! (VOICE) before "ji" attaches -- root "uqaq" (very common) has no
! reduced spelling of its own, so the conversion has to happen on ji's
! side, same VOICE-prefixed-candidate shape as juq/1vn's own "VOICEtu"
! elsewhere in this file. The literal is "ti" (own j ALREADY converted
! to t), not "ji" -- VOICE resolves early in phonology.xfscript's rule
! cascade, well BEFORE the general j->t rule at the very top, so
! "VOICEji" would never actually see "r" adjacent to "j" in time for
! that rule to fire (confirmed via a failed hfst-lookup attempt with
! "VOICEji" first: produced "uqarjii", j unconverted). Baking the t
! directly into the literal sidesteps the ordering issue entirely, same
! as juq/1vn's own "VOICEtu" already does. Not decomposable by the real
! Java analyzer either (confirmed via --pipeline).
++ji+1vn:VOICEti NounContinuations ;

! "jjut"/1vn ("reason/cause/motive for doing s.t."): same "one who/reason
! for X" shape as "ji"/1vn just above, wired identically (bare "jjut"
! terminal, continuing "jjuti", same 4 continuations). "katimajjutiksaq"
! also needed a bare (non-SUPPR) terminal candidate for ksaq/1nn below --
! own trailing q kept, since gold wants "ksaq" not "ksa" when it's the
! FINAL morpheme. q-context ("rut"/"ruti", Fusion) not attempted: no gold
! word in this cluster needs it.
++jjut+1vn:jjut # ;
++jjut+1vn:jjut NounContinuations ;
++jjut+1vn:jjuti NounContinuations ;

! "gaq"/1vn: "makpigaq" = {makpi:makpiq/1v}{gaq:gaq/1vn} -- verb-to-noun
! derivational suffix ("forms a noun with an inherently passive
! meaning"). Same shape as juq/1vn and kkut/1nn: Suffixes.csv's row has
! one deterministic candidate per context (V-form/action Neutral,
! t/k/q-form Suppression, all literally "gaq" itself unchanged) --
! genuine rule, reuses the existing SUPPR marker exactly like
! "liri"/"qai"/"kkut" (delete the preceding stem's final q/k/t,
! "makpiq"->"makpi", then append "gaq"). Also continues into NnSuffixes
! ("maligaksait" needs "ksaq"/1nn to attach directly after "gaq"), into
! NounEndings directly ("maligarmut"/"maligarmi"/"maligarmik"/
! "maligarnit" all attach a tn-ending directly onto "gaq" with no
! intervening "ksaq", reaching the generic non-trigger Lever A branch
! there -- confirmed by the attested surface "gar", Nasalization, not
! "ga", Suppression, since "gaq"/1vn is not one of Lever A's trigger
! ids), and into NvSuffixes (so a noun-to-verb suffix like "liuq" can
! follow: "maligaliuqti" = mali(malik/1v)+ga(gaq/1vn)+liuq(liuq/1nv)+
! ti(ji/1vn)).
++gaq+1vn:SUPPRgaq # ;
++gaq+1vn:SUPPRgaq NounContinuations ;

! "usiq"/1vn ("custom/way/habit"): Suffixes.csv's q-form lists three
! candidates ("usiq"/"usiq"/"qusiq") with actions Suppression/Voicing/
! Neutral -- but gold reveals SIX distinct literal spellings are actually
! needed, not three, because usiq's own trailing q behaves differently
! depending on what FOLLOWS it (own q kept bare, own q deleted, own q
! converted to r) -- the CSV under-lists the real variation. All six are
! wired as parallel literal spellings (different strings, no collision),
! each also carrying its own SUPPR prefix to delete the PRECEDING root's
! trailing q where gold needs that ("uqaq" family) -- except the
! "q"-prefixed trio (qusiq/qusi/qusir), which do NOT delete the preceding
! q, matching the "apiq" family's doubled-q surface ("apiqqusi..."013).
! Confirmed via:
!   - "uqausiq" (bare terminal): uqaq's own q deleted (SUPPR) + "usiq"
!     kept whole -- SUPPRusiq -> "#".
!   - "uqausiqtigut": same SUPPRusiq, reaching "tigut"/tn-via-p (which has
!     no SUPPR of its own, so usiq's own q must survive here too).
!   - "uqausiit"/"uqausiksait"/"uqausiksangit"/"uqausikkut"/
!     "uqausilirinirmut": SUPPRusiq would ALSO work here (the following
!     ending's own SUPPR eats usiq's trailing q for free), but "uqausinga"/
!     "uqausingit" need usiq's own q gone even though "nga" carries no
!     SUPPR marker at all -- so a genuinely separate "SUPPRusi" (own q
!     already gone) candidate is needed; wired uniformly rather than
!     picking per-word which of SUPPRusiq/SUPPRusi would happen to work.
!   - "uqausirmik"/"uqausirnik"/"uqausirnut": own q converted to r
!     (SUPPRusir) -- mik/nik/nut all already have their own bare/NASAL/
!     SUPPR variants from Lever A, and it's the BARE one that matches here
!     (SUPPRusir + bare "mik" = "usirmik").
!   - "apiqqusiit"/"apiqqusiksait": "qusiq" (own q kept, preceding q also
!     kept -- doubled "qq") -- the following SUPPR-marked ending eats
!     qusiq's own trailing q the same way as the uqaq family.
!   - "apiqqusirnut": "qusir" (own q -> r, preceding q kept).
!   - "apiqqusira"/"apiqqusirijara": would need "qusi" reaching
!     "ga"/tn-nom-s-1s and "gi"/1nv respectively -- both remain unreached
!     for other reasons (see "gi"/1nv's own comment below).
! "uqausirijanga"/"uqausissangit"/"uqausitsangit"/"uqausituinnakkut" also
! remain unreached: the first needs "jaq"/1vn chained after "gi"/1nv
! (gi's own continuations don't reach jaq yet), the middle two need
! "ssaq"/"tsaq" spelling variants of ksaq/1nn that don't exist, the last
! needs checking whether "tuinnaq"/2nn and "kkut"/1nn chain together the
! way this word needs -- none blocked by usiq itself, all separate small
! gaps left for a future pass.
++usiq+1vn:SUPPRusiq # ;
++usiq+1vn:SUPPRusiq NounContinuations ;
++usiq+1vn:SUPPRusi NounContinuations ;
++usiq+1vn:SUPPRusir NounContinuations ;
++usiq+1vn:qusiq # ;
++usiq+1vn:qusiq NounContinuations ;
++usiq+1vn:qusi NounContinuations ;
++usiq+1vn:qusir NounContinuations ;

! "ut"/1vn ("object/instrument/tool for doing s.t."): Suffixes.csv's
! V-form alone lists 12 space-separated candidates. Tracing every gold
! word's FULL decomposition chain instead shows it's the same "CSV under/
! over-lists, gold reveals the real literal-spelling set" shape as usiq
! above, just with MORE candidates because "ut" genuinely has three
! parallel sub-families, not one:
!   - V-context, own trailing q handled by SUPPR (root already q-final,
!     e.g. "ikajuq"): SUPPRut (bare terminal, "ikajuutit"), SUPPRuti
!     (continuing), SUPPRutik (alt bare terminal), SUPPRutaq (alt bare
!     terminal, own q survives unless a FOLLOWING SUPPR-marked ending eats
!     it -- "iksivautaq" bare vs "iksivautaup" via up/tn-gen-s's own SUPPR,
!     same "downstream SUPPR reduces utaq->uta for free" trick as usiq).
!   - q-prefix family (preceding root's own q is KEPT, doubled "qq" --
!     "apiq" family): qut/quti/qutik, no SUPPR at all, mirrors usiq's
!     qusiq/qusi/qusir treatment exactly.
!   - r-prefix family (preceding root's own trailing q IS deleted, by
!     ut's OWN SUPPR -- "giaq"/1vv and "liuq"/1nv's output): SUPPRrut
!     (bare terminal, "ilagiarut"), SUPPRruti (continuing,
!     "ilagiaruti"/"qaujigiarutit" -- "qaujigiarutit" needs bare SUPPRrut
!     + it, not SUPPRruti; both "rut"+it and "ruti"+it are gold-attested
!     free variants, same "apiqqutit"/"apiqqutiit" doubling seen in the
!     q-prefix family too).
!   - V-context gemination family: the CSV's own V-form actually lists
!     "jjut jjuti jjutik jjutaq" a SECOND time via action1 "i(jj)"
!     (Insertion of doubled "j") -- this IS the "mysterious jj-prefixed
!     spelling" this comment used to describe as "not in the CSV's own
!     candidate list at all" (round 22-era investigation missed it,
!     mistaking it for the separate, genuinely distinct "jjut"/1vn
!     suffix, Suffixes.csv nb=1 "reason/cause/motive", instead). Baked
!     directly into the literal text (same "unconditional insertion"
!     treatment as lugu/lugit's own "i(l)" case), not a marker: confirmed
!     against the REAL Java analyzer's own output (`{jjuti:ut/1vn}` for
!     "aulajjutinut") before wiring, not guessed. The plain (ungeminated)
!     "gut/guti/gutik/gutaq" V-context family (same row, action1 "n") is
!     wired alongside it for the same reason -- different strings, no
!     collision, gold may need either.
! NOT attempted (each a separate, smaller gap, not blocked by "ut"
! itself): "tn-nom-s-1s"/"ga" and "tn-nom-d"/"a-k" (whole unimplemented
! endings, block "apiqqutiga"/"iksivautaa" families); "ssaq"/"tsaq"
! spelling variants of ksaq/1nn (blocks "apiqqutissait"/
! "apiqqutitsait"); a bare "p"-only candidate for up/tn-gen-s (blocks
! "iksivautap"); "matu"+"iq"/1nv's own chain (blocks "matuirutimut",
! unverified whether iq/1nv even reaches here yet); "atiliurutausimajut"
! (already blocked upstream by liuq/1nv's unimplemented third spelling,
! see liuq's own comment below); "katimautiminingit"/"katimautinik"/
! "katimautitsa" and "naasautaa"/"naasautiit"/"naasautik"/"naasautilik"
! and "parnaut"/"parnautiit"/"parnautinik" and "uqaalautaa" and
! "uuktutigilugu" family -- all involve roots or preceding suffixes
! ("naasaq"/1v, "parnaq"/1v, "allak"/1vv, "uuk"+"tuq"/1vv chains) not
! individually re-verified; likely mostly reachable already given "ut"'s
! mechanism is now in place, worth re-checking with
! next_affix_priority.py/full_corpus_check.py rather than assumed
! working.
++ut+1vn:SUPPRut # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRut NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRuti # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRuti NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRutik # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRuta # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRuta NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRutaq # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRutaq NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:qut # ;
++ut+1vn:qut NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:quti # ;
++ut+1vn:quti NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:qutik # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRrut # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRrut NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRruti # ;
++ut+1vn:SUPPRruti NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:jjut # ;
++ut+1vn:jjut NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:jjuti # ;
++ut+1vn:jjuti NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:jjutik # ;
++ut+1vn:jjutaq # ;
++ut+1vn:jjutaq NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:gut # ;
++ut+1vn:gut NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:guti # ;
++ut+1vn:guti NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:gutik # ;
++ut+1vn:gutaq # ;
++ut+1vn:gutaq NounContinuations ;

! Suffixes.csv's own V-form column lists "ut uti utik utaq" TWICE --
! once (Neutral) as this family's plain, unmarked candidates, once more
! (further down the same cell) with action "i(jj)" for the already-
! wired "jjut/jjuti/jjutik/jjutaq" family above. Only the "g"-inserted
! sibling ("gut/guti/gutik/gutaq") and the "jj"-geminated one got wired
! when this suffix was first built -- the genuinely bare, unmarked
! forms were missed entirely. "katimautitsa" needs "uti" bare (no "g"),
! confirmed via gold; not decomposable by the real Java analyzer either
! (confirmed via --pipeline).
++ut+1vn:ut # ;
++ut+1vn:ut NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:uti # ;
++ut+1vn:uti NounContinuations ;
++ut+1vn:utik # ;
++ut+1vn:utaq # ;
++ut+1vn:utaq NounContinuations ;

! "jaq"/1vn: Suffixes.csv actually has TWO "jaq/1vn"-tagged rows (nb=1
! "passive", nb=3 "similar to"), distinguished only by an id-conditional
! condPrec (nb=1: NOT preceded by u/1nv; nb=3: preceded by u/1nv) -- but
! unlike the "mut"/"nik" id-conditional cases (deferred because the
! SURFACE FORM itself differs by condition), here both rows produce the
! IDENTICAL surface rule (V-form "jaq"/Neutral, t/k/q-form "taq"/Neutral
! -- the existing j->t-after-t/k/q rule handles the consonant contexts
! already, no new marker needed), so the id-conditional distinction is
! purely semantic and doesn't affect which lexc entry to write. "jaq"
! also gained its own t/k/q-context literal spelling, "taq" -- Suffixes.csv
! gives this directly as its own candidate (not derived via the general
! j->t rule), needed for "pigiaqtitaq" family ("tit"/1vv ends in t, jaq
! attaches right after) -- and a NnSuffixes continuation
! ("qaujimajatuqanginnik" needs jaq -> tuqaq/1nn directly). "ilagijaujuq"
! = {ila:ila/1n}{gi:gi/1nv}{jaq:jaq/1vn}{u:u/1nv}{juq:juq/1vn} needs the
! bare terminal path too ("piqujaq"), not just mid-chain.
++jaq+1vn:jaq NounContinuations ;
++jaq+1vn:jaq # ;
++jaq+1vn:taq NounContinuations ;
++jaq+1vn:taq # ;

! "saqqitaujuq" family (root "saqqik", k-final): "taq" above still spells
! its own trailing q, but the general (unmarked) k->t assimilation rule
! ALSO fires on the newly-created root-k/suffix-t boundary once "taq"
! attaches, over-applying into a spurious geminate ("saqqittaq" instead
! of gold's "saqqitaq") -- confirmed via direct hfst-lookup before
! wiring. What's actually needed is SUPPR (delete the root's own final
! k first) plus jaq's own q ALSO dropped ("ta"), the same shape as this
! round's juq/1vn "tu" fix -- avoids the k/t boundary ever forming, so
! the blanket rule has nothing to over-fire on.
++jaq+1vn:SUPPRta NounContinuations ;
++jaq+1vn:SUPPRta # ;

! "vik"/3vn ("place where the action of the verb happens"): q-context:
! "ilinniarvik" = {ilinniar:ilinniaq/1v}{vik:vik/3vn}, root's own
! trailing q rewritten to r (Voicing, same "marker-scoped rewrite" shape
! as NASAL but its own table -- new VOICE marker, phonology.xfscript).
! Only the q-context (single candidate, Voicing) and the terminal/
! NounEndings paths are wired: V-context is a genuine 2-candidate
! ambiguity (Suffixes.csv V-form "vik vik", action "i(p) n", no
! disambiguator) and k-context has TWO gold-attested surface variants for
! the same underlying word ("ikupigvilirijikkut" vs "ikupivvilirijikkut")
! which look like genuine dialectal alternates, not modeled here -- both
! left deferred rather than guessed at. Also gained an NvSuffixes
! continuation, needed for "aanniaviliaqtunut" (...+vi(vik/3vn)+
! liaq(2nv)+tu(juq/1vn)+nut) -- NOT reused via the existing VOICE-marked
! candidate: "aanniaq"(q-final) needs its own q DELETED here (SUPPR), not
! converted to r like "ilinniarvik" needed -- root-specific free
! variation, same as elsewhere in this file. "SUPPRvi" also bakes in
! vik's own trailing k already dropped (needed directly before liaq, a
! plain literal with no SUPPR of its own).
++vik+3vn:VOICEvik # ;
++vik+3vn:VOICEvik NounContinuations ;
++vik+3vn:SUPPRvi NounContinuations ;

! Two more free-variant spellings, own "v" doubled instead of the
! preceding consonant being voiced/deleted: "vvik" (own k kept,
! terminal) and "vvi" (own k dropped, continuing). Found via
! already-correct gold siblings: "pilirivik"/"piliriviit"/
! "pilirivinga" (single v) alongside the failing "pilirivvik"/
! "pilirivviit"/"pilirivvinga" (double v, identical decomposition
! each), and "ikupigvilirijikkut"/"ikupigvilirijikkunnut" (VOICE
! reading, k->g) alongside the failing "ikupivvilirijikkut"/
! "ikupivvilirijikkunnut" (SUPPR+double-v reading instead) -- so the
! k-deleting variant needs the SUPPR prefix too, same as "SUPPRvi"
! above.
++vik+3vn:vvik # ;
++vik+3vn:vvik NounContinuations ;
++vik+3vn:vvi NounContinuations ;
++vik+3vn:SUPPRvvik NounContinuations ;
++vik+3vn:SUPPRvvi NounContinuations ;

! "niq"/2vn: "qimirruniq" = {qimirru:qimirru/1v}{niq:niq/2vn} (V-context,
! plain concatenation) and "ilinniarniq" = {ilinniar:ilinniaq/1v}
! {niq:niq/2vn} (q-context: root's final "q" becomes "r"). Nasalization
! -- confirmed (Action.kt's Nasalization.surfaceForm() returns its input
! unchanged, i.e. same "marker, not text change" shape as Suppression;
! the real transformation lives in MorphAnalyzerValidation.kt's
! validate_nasalization_null, using Roman.nasalOfOcclusiveUnvoicedLat:
! k->"ng" ('N' internally), q->"r", t->"n", p->"m") -- genuinely
! deterministic, not corpus-disambiguated (unlike this same row's
! t-context, "niq niq" with two candidate actions "nas"/"s" and no
! algorithmic disambiguator -- skipped). New NASAL marker, same invisible-
! flag pattern as SUPPR/VVNG: k/q immediately before it get rewritten (not
! just deleted), then the marker itself is dropped. Also gained an
! own-q-deleted candidate, "ni" (needed for "matuiqtauninga" before
! "nga"/tn-nom-s-4s, which -- unlike "it"/"ngit"/etc -- carries no SUPPR
! of its own to do this for free), and a continuation beyond "#"
! (originally only ever validated as the word-final morpheme
! "qimirruniq"/"ilinniarniq" -- "tigusinirmut" needs "niq" to continue
! into "mut"; since "niq" is verb-to-noun, the noun-ending lexicon is the
! right continuation).
++niq+2vn:NASALniq # ;
++niq+2vn:NASALniq NounContinuations ;
++niq+2vn:NASALni NounContinuations ;

! Not implemented, revisit only if a real disambiguating condition turns
! up (in the source CSV or by tracing MorphAnalyzerValidation.kt) rather
! than picking the first-listed candidate by convention: "ut"/1vn's V/q
! candidate sets before the CSV-vs-gold investigation above resolved most
! of them -- Suffixes.csv's own row has 12 space-separated V-form
! candidates and 12 more q-form candidates with no condPrec or other
! disambiguating column; "ma"/1vv -- every context lists TWO full
! candidates ("ma"/"uma") with matching actions and no condition
! selecting between them (see "ma"/1vv's own comment in VvSuffixes below
! for how gold ultimately resolved this one anyway).

LEXICON NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix
++ni+tn-loc-p:SUPPRni # ;

! "nut"/tn-dat-p ("ajjigiinngittunut", same trigger list) and
! "tigut"/tn-via-p ("avittuqsimajutigut", same juq trigger). tigut's OWN
! CSV row files this conditional under its k-form column, not q --
! almost certainly a data-entry quirk (juq/1vn always surfaces q-final in
! every one of ITS OWN contexts, so a following morpheme can never see it
! as literally k-final), not a real k-context; implemented by what the
! mechanism clearly IS (juq-triggered Suppression), not by the column
! label, and confirmed correct against the one gold word that exercises
! it.
++tigut+tn-via-p:SUPPRtigut # ;

LEXICON NvSuffixes

! "it"/3nv ("to be such"): Suffixes.csv's own condPrec ("type:a") is a
! grammatical-feature condition the bulk generator can't model, but
! it's confirmed directly by gold: both target words' root is tagged
! "1a" (adjective), matching this row's own condition exactly.
! Q-context gives 2 candidates, both literal "it" with Suppression --
! no real ambiguity (both actions identical), resolves to a single
! "SUPPRit" (for the plain q-kept "qanuq" root spelling). A plain "it"
! (no marker) is ALSO needed since "qanuq"/1a already has its own
! q-dropped spelling variant "qanu" wired separately -- attaching to
! THAT spelling needs no further deletion. Previously investigated and
! confirmed low-value on its own (round-16-era: only 3 gold words are
! 3nv-tagged at all) but 2 of those 3 are exactly this suffix's own
! target words, so worth wiring now that they're the last remaining
! gap. Neither is decomposable by the real Java analyzer either
! (confirmed via --pipeline).
++it+3nv:it VerbContinuations ;
++it+3nv:SUPPRit VerbContinuations ;

! li/4vv ("to make that s.t. or s.o. become such") has condPrec
! "id:it/3nv" -- Suffixes.csv's own single-id trigger condition,
! wired the same way as the mut/nngit/u/juq triggers above and below
! (generate_affixes.py's TRIGGER_LEXICON): li/4vv is now reachable
! ONLY via AfterItTriggerSuffix, not from the general VerbContinuations
! hub it used to reach through the *Speculative lexicon (which is
! reachable from every verb stem, not just after it/3nv specifically).
++it+3nv:it AfterItTriggerSuffix ;
++it+3nv:SUPPRit AfterItTriggerSuffix ;

! "uq"/1nv ("to go through", the "via"-case-only sibling suffix):
! Suffixes.csv's own condPrec ("cas:via") is a grammatical-feature
! condition the bulk generator can't model in general, but it directly
! names the same case "tigut"/tn-via-p already marks -- t-context only
! (V/k/q are all "-", no candidate at all), Suppression (delete the
! preceding "tigut"'s own trailing t). "tigut"/tn-via-p (NounEndings
! above) previously had no continuation past its own bare terminal;
! gained one here specifically so "uq"/1nv can attach -- confirmed via
! "tusaajitiguuqtuq"/"tusaajitiguurunniiqtuq" (the latter also needs
! "uq"'s own trailing q dropped when junniiq/1vv's existing
! "SUPPRrunniiq" candidate follows -- already wired, no extra piece
! needed there) and the real Java analyzer's own output before wiring.
++uq+1nv:SUPPRuq VerbContinuations ;

++liri+1nv:SUPPRliri VerbContinuations ;

! "giik"/2nv: "ajjigiinngittunik" = {ajji:ajji/1n}{gii:giik/2nv}
! {nngit:nngit/1vv}{tu:juq/1vn}{nik:nik/tn-acc-p} -- V-context only
! (V-form=giik/Neutral). t-context is a genuine single candidate
! (Insertion "i") but unused here (root "ajji" is vowel-final);
! k/q-contexts use the unbuilt Fusion primitive, skipped.
++giik+2nv:giik VerbContinuations ;

! "liaq"/2nv ("motion towards: to go to"): clean single V-context
! candidate per Suffixes.csv (Neutral, bare "liaq"); "aanniaviliaqtunut"
! attaches after vik/3vn (vowel-final surface).
++liaq+2nv:liaq VerbContinuations ;

! "maligaliurviliarsimajut" needs a SECOND spelling, "liar" (own q->r,
! a free variant not derived from any general rule -- same "different
! literal spellings" category as naq/1vv's own "nar"), reached with
! SUPPR since root "maligaliurvik" (k-final) has its own trailing k
! dropped first. The root itself is no longer excluded -- it's been
! reachable since the CommonCompositeWords.csv skip_if_combination
! filter was removed earlier this session (re-tested and found to
! LOWER the false-positive count, not raise it), so the original
! "adding the root risks amplifying a collision" concern no longer
! applies; only this suffix-side piece was still missing. Not
! decomposable by the real Java analyzer either (confirmed via
! --pipeline).
++liaq+2nv:SUPPRliar VerbContinuations ;

! "iq"/1nv: clean single V-context candidate per Suffixes.csv (Neutral,
! bare "iq"); its own trailing q survives until something downstream
! needs it gone (si/1vv's own literal spellings and ut/1vn's SUPPR-
! prefixed "ruti" both already handle that, same established pattern as
! every other q-final suffix). t/k/q-context (Insertion "ng"/"a",
! Suppression) not attempted: unattested in this cluster.
++iq+1nv:iq VerbContinuations ;

! "liuq"/1nv ("to be building/working on s.t."): gaq/1vn's own SUPPR only
! deletes what PRECEDES gaq (malik's own final consonant) -- gaq's OWN
! trailing "q" survives ("maligaq" bare, "malik"+"gaq"). So liuq attaches
! to a Q-FINAL stem here, not a vowel-final one as it first looked from
! the surface alone: liuq needs ITS OWN SUPPR marker to delete gaq's
! trailing q. Suffixes.csv's q-form gives "liuq"/"jjiuq" (both
! Suppression) as the two listed candidates -- but gold ALSO attests
! "liur" (q -> r) for the exact same context, a candidate this CSV row
! doesn't list anywhere at all ("maligaliurti" alongside "maligaliuqti",
! same preceding "ga", same following "ti"/ji -- genuine free variation).
! Same "wire both literal spellings in parallel" treatment as
! ngagut/agut above: "SUPPRliuq" and "SUPPRliur" are different strings
! once SUPPR resolves, so no extra rule needed -- whichever the real
! word's own spelling is picks the matching path. "jjiuq" not attempted:
! unattested in this gold cluster. V+k contexts (V-form=liuq/Neutral,
! k-form=liuq/Suppression) alone, without the q-context above, are not
! independently gold-attested here: every gold example attaches liuq
! directly after a q-final suffix.
++liuq+1nv:SUPPRliuq VerbContinuations ;
++liuq+1nv:SUPPRliur VerbContinuations ;

! "qaq"/1nv ("to have/possess"), needed by "jjut"/1vn's "pijjutiqaqtu*"
! cluster -- clean single V-context candidate (Neutral), reused unchanged
! for t/k/q since "jjuti" (what it always attaches to here) is
! vowel-final. Needs BOTH VnSuffixes (for "juq"/1vn to follow,
! "pijjutiqaqtuq"/"...tunik") and TvEndings directly ("pijjutiqaqtut"
! attaches "jut"/tv-ger-3p straight onto qaq, no juq/1vn in between). A
! second gold example, "akiqangittuq", is NOT reached: it produces
! "akiqaNNgittuq" (double n) from plain concatenation + SUPPR, not gold's
! "akiqaNgittuq" (single n) -- something reduces nngit's own doubled "nn"
! to a single "n" specifically after qaq's deletion, not explained by any
! mechanism built so far (same unexplained-surface-simplification
! category as "iglu"->"illu"). Not pursued further; revisit once the
! nn->n reduction is understood.
++qaq+1nv:qaq VerbContinuations ;

! "gi"/1nv ("have as; possess"): "isumagillugu" = {isuma:isuma/1n}
! {gi:gi/1nv}{llugu:lugu/tv-part-1s-3s-prespas}. V-context only
! (V-form=gi/Neutral); t-context is a genuine single candidate too
! (Insertion "i") but unused by this word (root "isuma" is vowel-final)
! and not implemented (would need its own marker, deferred); k/q-contexts
! use "Fusion", an unbuilt primitive, skipped. Also gained its own
! q-context literal spelling, "ri" (Suffixes.csv gives this directly as a
! Fusion candidate -- mechanically identical to SUPPR, deletes the
! preceding q) -- needed for "apiqqusirijara" (usiq's own bare "qusiq"
! candidate, own q kept, then gi's "ri" eats it) -- and reaches
! VnSuffixes as well as TvEndings, so it can be followed by a further
! vn-suffix like "jaq"/1vn ("ilagijaujuq" needs gi -> jaq/1vn), not just
! terminate in a verb ending. "ut"/1vn's "quti" and "usiq"/1vn's "qusiq"
! candidates above both needed a path into NvSuffixes so "gi" can follow
! them at all -- neither had ever reached a noun-to-verb suffix before.
++gi+1nv:gi VerbContinuations ;
++gi+1nv:SUPPRri VerbContinuations ;

! "u"/1nv: "ministaujuq" = {minista:minista/1n}{u:u/1nv}{juq:juq/1vn} and
! "piliriangujuq" = {piliria:piliriaq/1n}{ngu:u/1nv}{juq:juq/1vn}.
! Suffixes.csv's "u" row has action1+action2 in every context, same shape
! as tn-nom-p's "it" -- confirmed (by tracing MorphAnalyzerValidation.kt)
! this is a genuine algorithmic condition, not lexically arbitrary
! ambiguity: "ng" is epenthesized before "u" whenever the stem left
! behind (after any q/k-deletion) ends in two vowels in a row (avoiding a
! 3-vowel run), and stays absent otherwise. V-context has no deletion
! (minista -> ministau); k/q-context deletes first, same as "liri"/"qai"
! (piliriaq -> piliria, SUPPR), *then* the same VV-gated insertion check
! applies to what's left (piliria ends "ia" -> VV -> ng inserted ->
! piliriangu). New VVNG marker (phonology.xfscript) implements the
! insertion the same way SUPPR implements deletion: invisible flag +
! context rule + cleanup, not the vv/consonant text itself, so the
! trigger is exactly "two vowels precede", not tied to which two vowels.
! t-context is DELIBERATELY NOT implemented: it has two structurally
! different candidates (delete-t+insert-ng vs keep-t+insert-i) with no
! algorithmic condition anywhere in the code selecting between them --
! genuinely lexically arbitrary -- AND unattested in the gold-standard
! sample. Also reaches TvEndings directly (not just another verb-to-noun
! derivational suffix): "qujannamiingujutit" =
! {qujannamiik:qujannamiik/1a}{u:u/1nv}{jutit:jutit/tv-ger-2s} needs "u"
! to reach a verb ENDING, since "u" is itself noun-to-verb and the stem
! it produces should be able to take any verb ending, the same "every
! X-producing morpheme should reach the full X-continuation set" gap the
! NounContinuations/VerbContinuations hub was built to close.
++u+1nv:SUPPRVVNGu VerbContinuations ;
++u+1nv:SUPPRVVNGu AfterUTriggerSuffix ;

LEXICON NnSuffixes

! "giik"/1nn ("a pair of two; a group of three or more"): Suffixes.csv's
! own condPrec is a grammatical-feature condition the bulk generator
! can't model, but 2 gold words ("katujjiqatigiingit"/"katujjiqatigiit")
! confirm the V-context literal needs its own trailing k dropped before
! a further ending attaches ("gii", not "giik") -- same "own consonant
! dropped before a further suffix" pattern used throughout this
! session, confirmed via the real Java analyzer's own output before
! wiring.
++giik+1nn:gii NounContinuations ;

! "juaq"/1nn ("large; big"): completely unwired until now (the existing
! JGUARD/"-rjuaq" machinery only ever protected this SAME spelling as a
! ROOT-internal augmentative in place names, e.g. "tikirarjuaq", never
! wired it as its own SUFFIX). Suffixes.csv's V-form action is "i(r)"
! (Insertion of "r"), not modeled by the bulk generator (zero prior
! gold evidence) -- but "iglulirijirjuakkut"/"illulirijirjuakkut" (root
! variants iglu/illu) both confirm the exact surface needed: "r"
! inserted AND juaq's own trailing q dropped (a following "kkut"/1nn
! attaches directly), giving the literal "rjua" -- confirmed via the
! real Java analyzer's own output before wiring. Needs the SAME JGUARD
! protection generate_roots.py's protect_internal_j() already gives
! root spellings with this identical "r" + "j" adjacency (the general
! j->t rule has no morpheme-boundary awareness, so it would otherwise
! corrupt this literal's OWN internal "rj" into "rt" -- caught via a
! direct hfst-lookup check before trusting the plain "rjua" spelling).
++juaq+1nn:rJGUARDjua NounContinuations ;
++juaq+1nn:rJGUARDjua # ;

++kkut+1nn:SUPPRkkut NounContinuations ;
++kkut+1nn:SUPPRkkut # ;
++kkut+1nn:SUPPRkkut QParticles ;

! "innaq"/1nn ("exclusiveness: 'just', 'only'"): Suffixes.csv's own row
! has NO condition column, but every context's action2 is "i(ng)", a
! code generate_affixes.py doesn't handle yet (see round-checkpoint notes
! on innaq/2vv's identical gap) -- so this row currently produces ZERO
! candidates, not even the plain V-context one. "qaujimajuinnaugatta"
! (gold's only innaq/1nn example) needs its own trailing q dropped
! before "u"/1nv attaches ("inna", not "innaq") -- wired directly as a
! plain literal rather than guessing at "i(ng)"'s general semantics from
! one data point.
++innaq+1nn:inna NounContinuations ;

! "&iq"/1nn ("superlativeness, the most of all"): the "&" in the CSV's
! own morpheme spelling is a placeholder/notation artifact (same "&" seen
! in generate_roots.py's filtered-out root rows, e.g. "ak&a"), not a
! literal candidate: every gold example uses the row's SECOND candidate,
! "lliq", instead. Two further literal spellings needed beyond that:
! "lliq" (q kept, before "paaq"/1nn) and "llir" (own q->r, before
! "mi"/"mik"/tn-loc-s/tn-acc-s) -- same "wire both, let the input string
! pick" free-variation pattern as usiq/miik/naq elsewhere in this file
! (neither "paaq" nor "mi"/"mik" carry a marker of their own that would
! make this predictable from what follows). Canonical MUST stay literally
! "&iq" to match the gold standard's own id string -- confirmed lexc/xfst
! tolerate "&" in a tag without special meaning.
++&iq+1nn:lliq NounContinuations ;
++&iq+1nn:lliq # ;
++&iq+1nn:llir NounContinuations ;
++&iq+1nn:llir # ;

! "paaq"/1nn ("the most of all; big, very"), the suffix &iq's "lliq"
! family chains into -- clean single V-context candidate per its own CSV
! row.
++paaq+1nn:paaq NounContinuations ;
++paaq+1nn:paaq # ;

! "miuq"/1nn ("resident of a place name"): clean single V-context
! candidate per Suffixes.csv (Neutral, bare "miuq"). SUPPR reused so a
! following ending's own SUPPR marker (it/tn-nom-p, nut/tn-dat-p, both
! already SUPPR-equipped) eats miuq's own trailing q for free -- same
! established pattern as every other "own q survives until something
! downstream needs it gone" suffix in this file.
++miuq+1nn:miuq NounContinuations ;

! "limaaq"/1nn ("inclusiveness: all of" -- a DIFFERENT homograph than
! "limaaq"/2vv "ceaselessly" in VvSuffixes below): a clean, single-
! candidate rule (V-form Neutral, t/k/q-form Suppression, same shape as
! juq/kkut/gaq/lik) once "nut" had both its default NASAL and SUPPR
! q-context branches (see NounEndings above) -- confirmed via
! "inulimaanut" = {inu:inuk/1n}{limaa:limaaq/1nn}{nut:nut/tn-dat-p} and
! "kikkulimaanut"/"kikkulimaat" (the latter also exercising "it"'s
! existing DECAP mechanism unchanged: limaaq's own trailing q is deleted,
! leaving "...limaa" -- two vowels -- so DECAP correctly strips "it"'s
! own leading i, giving "...limaat"). Two other candidate words
! ("kanatalimaami", needs root "kanata" but the only bulk-generated
! homograph is tagged 2n not gold's 1n -- a pre-existing, already-
! documented root-homograph mismatch; "nunavulimaami", root "nunavut"
! isn't bulk-generated at all -- it only exists in Locations.csv, a
! source file generate_roots.py doesn't cover) are left unimplemented,
! blocked by those unrelated gaps, not by limaaq itself.
++limaaq+1nn:SUPPRlimaaq NounContinuations ;

! "ralaaq"/1nn ("small"): Suffixes.csv's V-form is a single clean
! candidate (Neutral, "ralaaq"), but ALL gold examples -- including the
! BARE terminal one ("katimajiralaa", no further suffix at all) -- show
! the trailing q absent. Not a conditional SUPPR-deletion like every
! other q-final suffix elsewhere in this file: the CSV's "ralaaq" is the
! canonical/dictionary citation form, but the actual literal surface text
! at every attested attachment point is just "ralaa", unconditionally.
! Implemented as a plain literal (no marker at all) rather than guessing
! at a delete-trigger that no example actually needs. "katimajiralaat"
! (truncated "t", not "it") falls out for free from the existing DECAP
! mechanism: "ralaa" ends in two vowels, the same trigger
! "kikkulimaat" already exercises.
++ralaaq+1nn:ralaa # ;
++ralaaq+1nn:ralaa NounContinuations ;

! "lik"/1nn ("possession: 'one with'"): "nanulik" = {nanu:nanuq/1n}
! {lik:lik/1nn} -- noun-to-noun. Same shape as juq/kkut/gaq: one
! deterministic candidate per context (V-form/action Neutral, t/k/q-form
! Suppression, "lik" itself unchanged) -- genuine rule, reuses SUPPR
! unchanged. Also continues into NounEndings ("nunalittinni" =
! nuna+li(lik/1nn)+ttinni(ptingni/tn-loc-s-1d)), not just the terminal
! path (matching "nanulik" standalone).
++lik+1nn:SUPPRlik # ;
++lik+1nn:SUPPRlik NounContinuations ;

! "aluk"/1nn ("largeness/impressiveness"): Suffixes.csv gives TWO
! V-context candidates ("aluk"/"aaluk", each with a secondary "i(ra)"
! insertion action) -- but no gold-attested word needs the "aaluk"/
! "i(ra)" branch at all, so only the plain "aluk" Neutral candidate is
! implemented. Needs the SUPPR marker even though "aluk" itself is
! Neutral in V-context: "akuni" (i-final) is genuine V-context, but
! "uqsu*"'s actual root is "uqsuq" (q-FINAL -- the gold surface span
! "uqsu" is already q-deleted, easy to misread as vowel-final from the
! surface alone) -- aluk's own k/q-form action1 IS "s" (Suppression), the
! same SUPPR marker used everywhere else in this lexicon, harmless as a
! no-op when nothing q/k/t-final actually precedes it (confirmed safe for
! "akunialuk"). "uqsualuit"/"uqsualuup" need NO further new mechanism:
! "it"/tn-nom-p and "up"/tn-gen-s already carry their own SUPPR marker
! (deletes a preceding q/k/t), so aluk's own trailing "k" is deleted by
! the EXISTING machinery the moment it reaches NounEndings -- confirmed
! "aluit"/"aluup" fall out for free, same "bulk mechanism pays off beyond
! the tested set" shape as several other suffixes in this file.
! "uqsualummut" needed one new general rule: k->m -- "mut"/tn-dat-s's
! existing plain-Neutral candidate alone would give literal "aluk"+"mut"
! = "alukmut", not gold's "alummut". This isn't documented anywhere in
! aluk's own CSV row (that row's V/t/k/q-form columns describe aluk's OWN
! shape depending on what PRECEDES it, not what follows it -- irrelevant
! to this specific gap). Empirically it's the same total-regressive-
! assimilation family as the existing t->m/k->t/p->t/t->n rules -- k
! assimilating to a following m, verified against this one gold example.
++aluk+1nn:SUPPRaluk NounContinuations ;
++aluk+1nn:SUPPRaluk # ;

! "tamaaq"/1nn: "arraagutamaat" = {arraagu:arraagu/1n}{tamaa:tamaaq/1nn}
! {t:it/tn-nom-p} -- own rule is trivial (all four contexts Neutral,
! plain concatenation, no marker of its own needed). But this word is
! what finally forced implementing "it"/tn-nom-p's long-deferred
! Selfdecapitation (decap): once tamaaq's own trailing q is deleted (by
! "it"'s SUPPR), the stem left behind is "arraagutamaa", ending in two
! vowels -- exactly the condition that triggers decap (it -> t). The
! DECAP marker lives on "it"'s own entry in NounEndings above, not here
! (verified in isolation first: a toy "arraagutamaaqSUPPRDECAPit" string
! composed through analogous rules produced "arraagutamaat" exactly
! before touching the real lexicon).
++tamaaq+1nn:SUPPRtamaaq NounContinuations ;

! "tuqaq"/1nn: "gavamatuqakkut" = {gavama:gavama/1n}{tuqa:tuqaq/1nn}
! {kkut:kkut/1nn} -- V-context only (V-form=tuqaq/Neutral). t-context has
! a genuine single candidate too (Insertion "i") but isn't needed by this
! word (root "gavama" is vowel-final) and isn't implemented here -- would
! need its own marker (insert "i" before a t-final stem), deferred.
! k/q-contexts are ambiguous (2 unconditioned candidates each), skipped
! as usual. Also gained a NounEndings continuation and its own q-context
! Suppression candidate (Suffixes.csv's own q-form gives "tuqaq tuqaq"/
! "n s" -- a second, SUPPR-prefixed candidate) -- both needed for
! "qaujimajatuqanginnik" (jaq's own trailing q deleted by tuqaq's SUPPR,
! then tuqaq -> nginnik/tn-acc-p-4s).
++tuqaq+1nn:tuqaq NounContinuations ;
++tuqaq+1nn:SUPPRtuqaq NounContinuations ;

! "kkanniq"/1nn ("additional, more") already has bulk-generated
! "kkanniq"/"kanniq" plain and SUPPR-prefixed candidates -- also needs
! a doubled-"i" spelling ("kkanniiq"), found via an already-correct
! gold sibling ("sulikkanniq" alongside the failing "sulikkanniiq",
! identical decomposition).
++kkanniq+1nn:kkanniiq # ;
++kkanniq+1nn:kkanniiq NounContinuations ;

! "ksaq"/1nn: "maligaksait" = {malik:malik/1v}{gaq:gaq/1vn}
! {ksaq:ksaq/1nn}{it:it/tn-nom-p} -- same shape as juq/kkut/gaq/lik/
! tuinnaq (single candidate per context: V-form Neutral, t/k/q-form
! Suppression), reuses SUPPR unchanged. Reached here via "gaq"/1vn's
! NnSuffixes continuation above. Continues into NounEndings so "it" can
! follow: checked this doesn't hit "it"'s deferred Selfdecapitation gap
! the way "tamaaq" did -- deleting ksaq's own trailing q leaves
! "maligaksa", ending in a consonant+vowel, not two vowels, so decap
! stays inert here. Also gained a bare terminal candidate (own trailing q
! kept) -- "katimajjutiksaq" needs "ksaq" itself, not "ksa", when it's
! the final morpheme of the word (no further SUPPR-marked ending follows
! to eat the q); reuses the same SUPPR prefix (deletes jjuti's own
! trailing consonant if any), harmless no-op here since "jjuti" ends in a
! vowel. And a continuation into NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix --
! "maligaksanit" needs "nit"/tn-abl-p's own trigger-branch (Suppression)
! reached right after "ksaq", since ksaq/1nn is one of the trigger ids
! for Lever A (see NounEndings above).
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRksaq NounContinuations ;
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRksaq NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix ;
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRksaq # ;

! "ksaq" also has two further literal spellings Suffixes.csv doesn't
! list at all: "ssaq" and "tsaq" (own leading "k" surfacing as "s"/"t"
! specifically when directly following a q-final suffix like "gaq"/1vn
! or "ut"/1vn's own q-prefix family -- gold attests BOTH spellings for
! the SAME underlying chain, e.g. "maligassaq"/"maligatsaq" from the
! identical malik+gaq+ksaq combination, and "apiqqutissait"/
! "apiqqutitsait" from ut/1vn's own "qut" family -- genuine free
! variation, same "CSV under-lists the real variation, wire both in
! parallel" treatment as usiq/ut/naq/miik elsewhere in this file. Same
! SUPPR prefix and same three continuations as the existing "ksaq"
! spelling above.
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRssaq NounContinuations ;
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRssaq NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix ;
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRssaq # ;
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRtsaq NounContinuations ;
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRtsaq NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix ;
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRtsaq # ;

! "katimautitsa" needs a further reduction of "tsaq" -- own trailing q
! ALSO dropped, word-final ("tsa"). SUPPR is a harmless no-op here
! (attaches after "uti", vowel-final, nothing for SUPPR to delete), so
! this reaches "katimautitsa" the same way "utitsaq" would, just
! without the trailing q. Not decomposable by the real Java analyzer
! either (confirmed via --pipeline).
++ksaq+1nn:SUPPRtsa # ;

! "tuinnaq"/2nn ("only/just/merely"): "kikkutuinnait" =
! {kikku:kikkut/1p}{tuinna:tuinnaq/2nn}{it:it/tn-nom-p} -- full V/t/k/q,
! same shape as juq/kkut/gaq/lik/raq (single candidate, Neutral/
! Suppression), reuses SUPPR. Continues into NounEndings (the
! "it"/tn-nom-p above) rather than back into NnSuffixes: checked that
! this doesn't hit "it"'s deferred Selfdecapitation gap (unlike the
! "limaaq"/1nn case above) -- deleting tuinnaq's own trailing q leaves
! "tuinna", ending in a single vowel after a consonant, not two vowels,
! so decap never fires here.
++tuinnaq+2nn:SUPPRtuinnaq NounContinuations ;

! Five more words, picked to cover every remaining decomposition-
! signature type (c, a, e, p, vv, tv) not otherwise exercised, after
! checking each new morpheme's phonology against the source CSVs the same
! way as every other entry in this file. All five checked out as genuine
! deterministic rules -- none needed a lexical-alternative fallback like
! the rejected "mata/mmata" case (an ambiguous, uncommitted candidate
! pair mentioned elsewhere in this project's own investigation notes).
!
!   - "ammattauq" = {amma:amma/1c}{ttauq:ttauq/1q} -- conjunction root +
!     enclitic particle, straight concatenation (amma is vowel-final, so
!     ttauq's V-form applies unchanged). No new rule.
!   - "ilaaqai" = {ilaa:ilaak/1e}{qai:qai/1q} -- exclamation root +
!     enclitic particle. qai's k-context row carries the same
!     Action.Suppression as liri's q-context row above: deletes the root's
!     final k. Reuses the (now-generalized) SUPPR marker/rule rather than
!     adding a k-specific one.
!   - "maanna" = {maanna:maanna/1a} -- adverb, single morpheme, no
!     phonology at all.
!   - "kina" = {kina:kina/1p} -- pronoun (from Pronouns.csv, a separate
!     file from RootsSpalding.csv), single morpheme, no phonology.
!   - "anginngittut" = {angi:angi/1v}{nngit:nngit/1vv}{tut:jut/tv-ger-3p} --
!     verb root + verb-to-verb negation suffix + verb ending. angi+nngit is
!     plain concatenation (angi is vowel-final, nngit's V-form applies
!     unchanged); nngit+jut->tut reuses the existing j->t-after-t/k/q
!     rule (nngit is t-final) -- no new rule needed for this word at all,
!     it's entirely covered by rules already validated on earlier words.

LEXICON Conjunctions
amma+1c:amma QParticles ;

! Two more spelling variants found by the same systematic root sweep
! as the Nouns block above: "uvalu" variant of "uvvalu"/1c; "uvvaluunni"
! variant of "uvvaluunniit"/1c (truncated, own trailing "it" dropped).
uvvalu+1c:uvalu QParticles ;
uvvaluunniit+1c:uvvaluunni QParticles ;

LEXICON Exclamations
ilaak+1e:ilaak QParticles ;

LEXICON QParticles
QParticlesGenerated ;
QParticlesGeneratedSpeculative ;
# ;
++ttauq+1q:ttauq # ;
++qai+1q:SUPPRqai # ;
++lu+1q:lu # ;

! Enclitic particles can stack ("taimaliqai" = li/1q then qai/1q) --
! each hand-authored particle above also gets a QParticles continuation
! alongside its "#" terminal, so a second particle can follow.
++ttauq+1q:ttauq QParticles ;
++qai+1q:SUPPRqai QParticles ;
++lu+1q:lu QParticles ;

! "lu"/1q: "ammalu" = {amma:amma/1c}{lu:lu/1q} -- V-context only
! (V-form=lu/Neutral). t/k/q-form is Voicing ("son") -- a single
! candidate ("lu" itself unchanged, so this rewrites the PRECEDING stem,
! same "marker not text change" shape as Suppression/Nasalization).
! Confirmed once the VOICE marker existed: "asingillu" =
! {asi:asi/1n}{ngil:ngit/tn-nom-p-4s}{lu:lu/1q}: "ngit"'s own trailing t
! (always literal "ngit", t-final) rewrites to l before "lu", giving
! "asingil"+"lu" = "asingillu". Same mechanism confirmed via
! "asinginnillu"/"asinginnullu" (nginnit/nginnut, also always t-final)
! and "inulirijikkullu" (kkut, likewise t-final). VOICElu is a SECOND,
! generic entry in the shared QParticles hub (not scoped per
! source-suffix) -- safe because VOICE is a no-op when nothing t/k/q
! precedes it, same as every other marker reused in a hub reachable from
! multiple contexts (e.g. SUPPR-marked entries already coexisting with
! plain ones throughout this file). ngit/nginnit/nginnut/kkut each needed
! a NEW continuation into QParticles (none of the four ever reached it
! before -- discourse particles like "-lu"/"-li" attaching after a
! fully-inflected noun is a general phenomenon, but only these four
! specific endings are wired here, matching this project's minimal-scope
! policy of wiring what a real gold word needs, not the fully general
! case).
++lu+1q:VOICElu # ;

! "li"/1q ("but"): "kisianili" = {kisiani:kisiani/1c}{li:li/1q} --
! V-only, same shape as "lu"/1q (t/k/q use the Voicing primitive; li's
! own t-context is NOT wired: no gold word in this lexicon's reach
! exercises it yet -- every candidate needs an unimplemented dependency,
! e.g. "apiqqutigali" needs "ut"/1vn's "ga"-continuation, which doesn't
! exist).
++li+1q:li # ;

LEXICON Adverbs

! Eight more spelling variants found by the same systematic root sweep
! as the Nouns block above: "asuillaak" variant of "asuilaak"/1a
! (double "l"); "atsualuk" variant of "aksualuk"/1a; "immagaa"/"immaqa"
! variants of "immaqaa"/1a; "ippaksaq"/"ippassaq"/"ippatsaq" variants
! of "ikpaksaq"/1a (three parallel candidates, same free-variation
! shape as everywhere else in this file); "qanu" variant of "qanuq"/1a
! (own trailing q dropped); "qujannamii" variant of
! "qujannamiik"/1a (own trailing k dropped); "surlu" variant of
! "suurlu"/1a; "uattiaru" variant of "uattiaruk"/1a (own trailing k
! dropped).
asuilaak+1a:asuillaak NounContinuations ;
aksualuk+1a:atsualuk NounContinuations ;
immaqaa+1a:immagaa NounContinuations ;
immaqaa+1a:immaqa NounContinuations ;
ikpaksaq+1a:ippaksaq NounContinuations ;
ikpaksaq+1a:ippassaq NounContinuations ;
ikpaksaq+1a:ippatsaq NounContinuations ;
qanuq+1a:qanu NounContinuations ;
qujannamiik+1a:qujannamii NounContinuations ;
suurlu+1a:surlu NounContinuations ;
uattiaruk+1a:uattiaru NounContinuations ;

maanna+1a:maanna # ;

! "maanna" needs a continuation into NvSuffixes (for "u"/1nv to follow,
! "maannaujumi") -- adverbs had only ever continued to "#" before
! (matching "maanna" read standalone).
maanna+1a:maanna NounContinuations ;

! "qujannamiik" ("thank you!", CommonCompositeWords.csv, hand-added same
! reasoning as "qaujima"/"iqqanaijaq" in Verbs above) needs a continuation
! into NvSuffixes (for "u"/1nv to follow, in "qujannamiingujutit").
qujannamiik+1a:qujannamiik NounContinuations ;

! "taimanna" (already bulk-generated in AdverbsGenerated, terminal-only)
! needs the SAME NvSuffixes continuation added here for "taimannaummat" =
! {taimanna:taimanna/1a}{u:u/1nv}{mmat:mat/tv-caus-4s} -- "u"/1nv already
! reaches TvEndings, just never had an adverb able to reach IT before. A
! second lexc entry for the same morpheme+tag (one from AdverbsGenerated
! terminal-only, one hand-authored here with the extra continuation) is
! fine, same "multiple paths to the same morpheme" pattern as
! sima/tuq/juma's own multi-continuation TvEndings/VnSuffixes entries in
! VvSuffixes below.
taimanna+1a:taimanna NounContinuations ;

! Demonstrative spelling variants Demonstratives.csv doesn't record at
! all (that file has no "variant" column, unlike the root-source CSVs
! generate_roots.py reads) -- found the same way as "iglu"/"illu"
! above, by listing every gold word using these roots: "tagva"/ad-sc
! ("right here beside me", standalone) and "tagv"/rad-sc (its own
! root-taking-an-ending form, e.g. "tagv"+"ani"/tad-loc = "tagvani")
! are both attested with a "tavv"-spelled variant too ("tavva"
! standalone; "tavani"/"tavvani" alongside canonical "tagvani" for the
! SAME root+ending pair) -- free spelling variation, not a conditioned
! alternation (same trap "iglu"/"illu" above was originally
! mis-suspected of).
tagva+ad-sc:tavva # ;
tagva+ad-sc:tavva QParticles ;
tagv+rad-sc:tav TadEndings ;
tagv+rad-sc:tavv TadEndings ;

! "uvva" spelling variant of "ubva"/ad-sc ("right here beside me" --
! yes, the SAME meaning as "tagva" above; two distinct demonstrative
! rows share it in Demonstratives.csv) -- same free-variation
! treatment, found the same way (gold attests "uvva" directly, no
! ending).
ubva+ad-sc:uvva # ;
ubva+ad-sc:uvva QParticles ;

! "tam" spelling variant of "tama"/rad-ml, needed for "tamani" =
! tama+ani/tad-loc: plain concatenation "tama"+"ani" would give
! "tamaani" (double a), but gold's own attested surface drops one --
! found via a systematic sweep of every gold demonstrative word
! against every currently-wired root+ending spelling combination
! (rather than hunting sub-clusters one at a time), same evidence-based
! variant treatment as everywhere else in this file, just for a single
! word this time (not enough other evidence to tell whether this is a
! general vowel-hiatus rule or root-specific).
tama+rad-ml:tam TadEndings ;

LEXICON Pronouns
kina+1p:kina NounContinuations ;

! "ivvit" spelling variant of "igvit"/1p ("you"), found by the same
! systematic root sweep as the Nouns block above -- a third spelling
! alongside the two already bulk-generated ("igvit"/"ipvit").
igvit+1p:ivvit NounContinuations ;

! "taapsu"/rpd-sc-s (root-taking-an-ending form behind "taamna"/
! pd-sc-s "this one right here") is attested with "taass"/"taats"
! spelling variants too (e.g. "taassuma"/"taatsuma" alongside canonical
! "taapsu"+"ma"/tpd-gen-s) -- same free-variation treatment as
! "tagv"/rad-sc above.
taapsu+rpd-sc-s:taassu TpdEndings ;
taapsu+rpd-sc-s:taatsu TpdEndings ;

! "tamaksu"/rpd-ml-s (a sibling root, same alternation) gets the same
! "ss"-spelled variant: "tamassuminga"/"tamassumunga" alongside
! canonical "tamaksu"+"minga"/"munga".
tamaksu+rpd-ml-s:tamassu TpdEndings ;

! Six more demonstrative spelling variants, all found the same
! systematic way (a sweep comparing every gold demonstrative word
! against every currently-wired spelling combination, instead of
! chasing individual sub-clusters): "taanna"/"tanna" variants of
! "taamna"/pd-sc-s ("this one right here", standalone); "taikua"
! variant of "taikkua"/pd-sc-p (single vs double "k"); "tainna"
! variant of "taingna"/pd-sc-s (the same "ngn"->"nn"-family
! simplification already seen for "kanangnaq"->"kanannaq"); "taissu"/
! "taitsu" variants of "taiksu"/rpd-sc-s (the same "ksu"->"ssu"/"tsu"
! alternation already confirmed for "taapsu"/"tamaksu" above -- a
! genuinely recurring pattern across every "-ksu"-final demonstrative
! root, not a one-off); "takkua" variant of "taakkua"/pd-sc-p (single
! vs double "a"); "taqqakku" variant of "taqqapku"/rpd-mlsc-p (p->k,
! matching the pku/kku split already visible as separate lexical items
! elsewhere in the generated demonstrative set).
taamna+pd-sc-s:taanna # ;
taamna+pd-sc-s:taanna QParticles ;
taamna+pd-sc-s:tanna # ;
taamna+pd-sc-s:tanna QParticles ;
taikkua+pd-sc-p:taikua # ;
taikkua+pd-sc-p:taikua QParticles ;
taingna+pd-sc-s:tainna # ;
taingna+pd-sc-s:tainna QParticles ;
taiksu+rpd-sc-s:taissu TpdEndings ;
taiksu+rpd-sc-s:taitsu TpdEndings ;
taakkua+pd-sc-p:takkua # ;
taakkua+pd-sc-p:takkua QParticles ;
taqqapku+rpd-mlsc-p:taqqakku TpdEndings ;

! "manna"/pd-ml-s (bulk-generated in demonstratives-generated.lexc,
! never hand-edited) only ever continued to "#"/QParticles -- gold
! attests it ALSO taking "u"/1nv ("mannaujuq" = manna+u+juq), the same
! "every X-producing morpheme should reach its full continuation set"
! gap already found and fixed for several other roots this session.
! Hand-added here as a parallel path rather than touching the
! generator (scoped to this one word, not re-checked against every
! other demonstrative root), confirmed via the real Java analyzer's
! own output before wiring.
manna+pd-ml-s:manna NvSuffixes ;

LEXICON VvSuffixes

! "gi"/4vv ("added to 'gi' verbs to use them transitively"):
! Suffixes.csv's own condPrec ("type:v,transinfix:gi/4vv") is a
! grammatical-feature condition the bulk generator can't model in
! general, but 2 gold words confirm exactly what's needed: V-context
! plain "gi" (Neutral, "kamagijalik") and q-context "ri" via Fusion
! (KNOWN_ACTION1 treats "fus" as SUPPR -- the CSV's own q-form literal
! already spells the substituted text, "ri" not "gi", same "rama"-not-
! "gama" precedent already documented for other Fusion rows;
! "ilitarijauningit" needs the root's own trailing q ALSO dropped via
! SUPPR) -- confirmed via the real Java analyzer's own output before
! wiring.
++gi+4vv:gi VerbContinuations ;
++gi+4vv:SUPPRri VerbContinuations ;

! "innaq"/2vv ("to do nothing but; exclusively"): Suffixes.csv's own
! action2 in every context is "i(ng)" (Insertion of "ng"), not modeled
! by the bulk generator -- but neither gold example shows any "ng" at
! all, so only the plain action1 (Neutral) literal is wired, same
! "ignore an unexplained action2" precedent as juq/1vn's/jaq/1vn's own
! unimplemented action2 codes elsewhere in this file.
! "katimajiralaanguinnaqtut" needs the bare V-context literal "innaq"
! (own q kept, since "jut"/tv-ger-3p follows); "aaqqiumainnarutinut"
! needs it with its OWN trailing q ALSO dropped ("inna", since
! "ut"/1vn follows) -- same "own q dropped before a further vowel-
! initial suffix" pattern used throughout this session (juq's "tu",
! jaq's "ta", mata's own literal, etc.), confirmed via the real Java
! analyzer's own output before wiring.
++innaq+2vv:innaq VerbContinuations ;
++innaq+2vv:inna VerbContinuations ;

! "i"/1vv ("antipassive-marking placeholder": keeps a transitive verb's
! transitive sense when followed by an intransitive infix/ending):
! Suffixes.csv's own condPrec ("antipassive:i/1vv") is a grammatical-
! feature condition the bulk generator can't model in general, but
! this SPECIFIC row is confirmed by direct cross-reference with
! tuq/1vv's own "antipassive" column (which literally names "i/1vv" as
! its partner) plus 2 gold words ("iqqaqtuivilirijikkut"/
! "iqqaqtuivilirijikkunnut") -- V-context only (Neutral, plain "i"),
! t/k/q-context (Suppression) left unwired for lack of any gold example.
++i+1vv:i VerbContinuations ;

! "si"/3vv ("added to 'gi'-verbs to make them intransitive" -- a sibling
! marker to "i"/1vv above, same shape): Suffixes.csv's own condPrec
! ("type:v,intransinfix:si/3vv") is a grammatical-feature condition the
! bulk generator can't model, but ALL FOUR contexts (V/t/k/q) give the
! identical literal "si" with Neutral action -- no marker needed at all,
! regardless of what precedes. "ilitaqsiniq" confirms this directly
! (root "ilitaq", q-final, still takes plain "si" unconverted), via the
! real Java analyzer's own output before wiring.
++si+3vv:si VerbContinuations ;

! "gusuk"/1vv ("intransitivizer, added to 'gi'-verbs" -- Suffixes.csv
! lists a 2nd row, nb=2, "to like/want to do s.t.", gated by the negated
! condition "!intransinfix:gusuk/1vv", but BOTH rows share the exact
! same V/t/k/q literal forms, so which sense applies doesn't affect the
! surface at all, same "condPrec doesn't change the wiring" precedent as
! jaq/1vn's own id-conditional case): V-context "gusuk" (Neutral),
! t-context "SUPPRgusuk" (Suppression, deletes the preceding root's own
! final consonant) -- "alianaigusukpunga" (root "alianait", t-final)
! confirms the t-context specifically, via the real Java analyzer's own
! output before wiring.
++gusuk+1vv:gusuk VerbContinuations ;
++gusuk+1vv:SUPPRgusuk VerbContinuations ;

! "allak"/1vv ("ease, simpleness of action: 'easily', 'just'"):
! Suffixes.csv gives 2 literal spellings in EVERY context ("allak"/"ala",
! same free-variation shape as usiq/ut/miik) -- only V-context wired so
! far since "uqaalautaa" (root "uqaq", V-context) is the only gold
! example, confirmed via the real Java analyzer's own output before
! wiring. The CSV's own action2 ("i(ra)", an insertion this project's
! generator doesn't model) is left unimplemented, same as juq/1vn's own
! unexplained action2 codes elsewhere in this file.
++allak+1vv:allak VerbContinuations ;
++allak+1vv:ala VerbContinuations ;

! t/k/q-context (Suppression, deletes the preceding stem's final q/k/t):
! same two literal spellings again, needed since "uqaalautaa"'s root
! "uqaq" is itself q-final (own q deleted by SUPPR before "ala"
! attaches).
++allak+1vv:SUPPRallak VerbContinuations ;
++allak+1vv:SUPPRala VerbContinuations ;

! "li"/2vv ("to make that s.t. or s.o. ..."): Suffixes.csv gives a clean
! single-candidate row per context (V "li" Neutral, t/k/q "li"
! Suppression), but its condPrec ("!cp(id:li/4vv)", a negated
! mutual-exclusion note against the DIFFERENT li/4vv homograph, not a
! blocking condition on li/2vv itself) isn't a bare "id:X" trigger the
! bulk generator understands -- "atuliqujaujuq" needs it (root "atuq"
! q-context: SUPPR deletes the q).
++li+2vv:li VerbContinuations ;
++li+2vv:SUPPRli VerbContinuations ;

! "ksaq"/2vv ("to find, consider s.t. or s.o. ..."): Suffixes.csv gives
! a clean single-candidate row per context (V "ksaq" Neutral, t/k/q
! "ksaq" Suppression), but its condPrec ("type:v,nature:a") is a
! grammatical-feature condition the bulk generator can't model, so it
! was never wired at all -- "naammasaqtuit"/"naammasaqtut" need it.
! SUPPR only ever deletes the PRECEDING stem's final q/k/t (as it does
! everywhere else in this lexicon), it does NOT touch the suffix's own
! leading "k" -- "SUPPRksaq" (below) still spells out the full "ksaq",
! it just also deletes the root's own final consonant first. What
! "naammasaqtuit"/"naammasaqtut" actually need is a THIRD candidate,
! SUPPR PLUS the suffix's own "k" dropped too ("SUPPRsaq", root
! "naamak"'s own doubled-m "naammak" spelling minus its trailing k),
! confirmed via the real Java analyzer's own output before wiring.
++ksaq+2vv:ksaq VerbContinuations ;
++ksaq+2vv:SUPPRksaq VerbContinuations ;
++ksaq+2vv:SUPPRsaq VerbContinuations ;

! "nngit"/1vv's own CSV row (Suffixes.csv) has Suppression, not Neutral,
! in the t/k/q contexts -- "nngit" was only ever tested after
! vowel-final "angi" ("anginngittut"), where SUPPR is a no-op either way,
! so the gap stayed invisible until a q-final stem ("qaq") needed to
! attach directly; fixed by adding the SUPPR marker. Its VnSuffixes
! continuation had a similar back-and-forth: removed once when its only
! justifying word ("akiqangittuq"/qaq) turned out blocked by an unrelated
! gap (see "qaq"/1nv's comment in NvSuffixes above), then restored once
! "ajjigiinngittunik" legitimately needed it (nngit -> juq/1vn).
++nngit+1vv:SUPPRnngit VerbContinuations ;
++nngit+1vv:SUPPRnngit AfterNngitTriggerSuffix ;

! "luaq"/1vv ("excessive action: too much/quite"): clean single
! V-context candidate per Suffixes.csv (Neutral, bare "luaq"; the row's
! second candidate, "lluaq", is unattested here). Reaches VnSuffixes for
! juq/1vn to follow ("piluaqtumi"/"...mik"/"...mit"). The last of these
! ("piluaqtumit") found one more gap: mit/tn-abl-s had never been added
! to NounEndingsAfterQTriggerSuffix, unlike its "mi"/"mik" siblings --
! fixed there.
++luaq+1vv:luaq VerbContinuations ;

! "vallia"/1vv ("progression, gradually") -- clean single V-context
! candidate per Suffixes.csv (Neutral, bare "vallia"); needed for
! "pivalliatittinirmut" (si/1vv's t-context "ti" family, via tit/1vv).
! t/k/q-form ("pallia", v->p, own literal spelling) not attempted:
! unattested in this corpus.
++vallia+1vv:vallia VerbContinuations ;

! "tuinnaq"/1vv ("merely/only/simply"): clean single V-context candidate
! per Suffixes.csv (Neutral, bare "tuinnaq"); every gold example attaches
! after an already-vowel-final vv-suffix (ma/juma/juma-via-ruma). A
! DIFFERENT homograph from the already-implemented "tuinnaq"/2nn noun
! suffix in NnSuffixes above -- confirmed genuinely separate tags before
! wiring, not a duplicate.
++tuinnaq+1vv:tuinnaq VerbContinuations ;

! "si"/1vv: revisiting an earlier "ABANDONED" verdict written when mut's
! id-conditional q-context was still the blocker. Suffixes.csv's 3
! candidate rows (nb 1/2/3) all show plain "si" in every context, but
! gold's "aulattijiit"/"pivalliatittinirmut" (t-final preceding morpheme)
! show si surfacing as "ti" -- an s->t change no CSV row documents (a
! direction of assimilation opposite this project's existing t->n/k->t/
! p->t family: here the SUFFIX's own initial consonant matches the
! PRECEDING one, not the reverse). Not guessed as a general rule -- wired
! as its own literal spelling, same "different strings, no collision"
! trick as every other multi-candidate suffix in this file.
! "tigusinirmut" (root "tigu", vowel-final) confirms plain "si" for the
! V-context case, and mut's own q-context (resolved by Lever A, see
! NounEndings above) produces "mut" correctly from "niq"+"mut" via the
! already-built default-branch mechanism. Every original blocker for
! this suffix turned out independently resolved by other mechanisms:
! mut's id-conditional q-context by Lever A, the "arjaq"/"ajjaq" root
! alternation by generate_roots.py's variant-column support, and "ti"
! wired directly as si's own literal spelling (never fully "explained",
! but empirically safe -- same policy as every other multi-candidate
! suffix in this file).
++si+1vv:si VerbContinuations ;
++si+1vv:ti VerbContinuations ;

! "naq"/1vv ("to cause/make"): Suffixes.csv's V-form gives 4 candidates
! (naq/naq/nak/nak, two with an Insertion action) but gold's actual
! "niqsunaqtuq"/"niqtunaqtuq"/"nirtunartuq" cluster shows just TWO real
! literal spellings needed: bare "naq" and its own q->r conversion "nar"
! -- both attested for the SAME root ("niqtuq" family) across different
! Hansard transcriptions, same free-variation shape as usiq/1vn and
! miik/1vn above. Wired as two plain literals (not a NASAL marker
! rewriting something else -- "nar" is naq's OWN alternate spelling, not
! a rewrite of what precedes it).
++naq+1vv:naq VerbContinuations ;
++naq+1vv:nar VerbContinuations ;

! "qujannami" needs a THIRD spelling, "nna" -- matches Suffixes.csv's
! own V-form row directly: 4 space-separated candidates ("naq naq nak
! nak"), the 2nd/4th pairing "i(n)" (Insertion of "n") with their own
! trailing q/k dropped, confirmed via the real Java analyzer's own
! output before wiring. "tukisinaliqtissimajuq" needs a related but
! DIFFERENT "na" spelling (n NOT doubled, own q also gone) -- still not
! attempted, a separate word to verify on its own.
++naq+1vv:nna VerbContinuations ;

! "tukisinaliqtissimajuq" needs the related but DIFFERENT "na" spelling
! (n NOT doubled, own q also gone) flagged above, confirmed via the
! real Java analyzer's own output before wiring.
++naq+1vv:na VerbContinuations ;

! "qu"/2vv ("to desire, to wish something to be done"): V-form Neutral,
! t/k/q-form Suppression -- same clean single-candidate shape as
! juq/kkut/gaq/lik/limaaq. "piqujaq" = {pi:pi/1v}{qu:qu/2vv}{jaq:jaq/1vn}
! -- V-context (root "pi" is vowel-final), continues into VnSuffixes
! since jaq/1vn follows it.
++qu+2vv:qu VerbContinuations ;

! "a"/1vv ("action done repeatedly/on several objects"): same
! "bare-terminal keeps q, continuing form drops it" shape as ut/1vn's own
! ut/uti split above: "atuagaq" (bare terminal) keeps "aq";
! "atuagait"/"atuagarmik"/"atuagarnik" (continuing into gaq/1vn) use the
! reduced "a". Root "atuq" is q-final (surfaces "atu"), so both
! candidates need SUPPR to delete it -- same trap as several other
! q-final-root suffixes in this file.
++a+1vv:SUPPRa VerbContinuations ;
++a+1vv:SUPPRaq # ;

! "juma"/1vv ("desire"): V-form is a genuine 2-candidate free-variation
! ambiguity ("juma"/"guma", both Neutral -- gold attests BOTH spellings
! for the identical decomposition, e.g. "qaujijumajunga" vs
! "qaujigumajunga", so implementing V-context would mean guessing, same
! policy as "ma"/1vv below); t-context is likewise 2-candidate, also
! skipped. ONLY the q-context is implemented: single candidate, Fusion
! (== SUPPR reused, literal text already substituted to "ruma" in the
! CSV, same shape as "gama"/"gapta"/"gavit"'s own Fusion rows in
! TvEndings below) -- confirmed via "uqarumajunga"/"uqarumavunga" (root
! "uqaq", q-final). Also reaches VvSuffixes directly (not just
! TvEndings): "tusarumatuinnaqtunga" = tusaq+ruma(juma q-context)+
! tuinnaq(1vv)+tunga.
++juma+1vv:SUPPRruma VerbContinuations ;

! "lauq"/1vv and "qqau"/1vv ("uqalaurmat"/"uqaqqaummat"): Suffixes.csv
! gives both a clean single-candidate shape, same as juma's q-context:
! V-form Neutral, t/k/q-form Suppression (deletes the preceding stem's
! own final q/k/t) -- only the q-context is implemented here since that's
! what both gold words need (root "uqaq", q-final). "lauq" has a SECOND
! row in Suffixes.csv (a different function, "priority of the command")
! gated by "condOnNext=mode:imp" -- a real disambiguator, not a guess:
! these target words aren't imperative, so the first row (general
! perceived past) is the unambiguous match. Both suffixes are themselves
! q-final, so "mat"/tv-caus-4s's own NASAL marker (see TvEndings below)
! turns THEIR trailing q into "r" when it directly follows --
! "uqalaurmat" is "uqa"+SUPPR(deletes uqaq's own q)+"lauq"+NASAL(lauq's q
! -> r)+"mat".
++lauq+1vv:SUPPRlauq VerbContinuations ;

! "giaq"/1vv ("begin to", needed by "ut"/1vn's r-prefix family above):
! Suffixes.csv gives a clean single V-context candidate (Neutral, bare
! "giaq") -- confirmed via "ilagiarut"/"qaujigiarutit", where giaq's own
! trailing q is deleted not by anything special here but by "ut"/1vn's
! OWN SUPPR marker on its r-prefixed candidate -- the same "the FOLLOWING
! suffix's SUPPR eats MY trailing q" pattern established for gaq/usiq
! above, not a new mechanism. Also reaches VvSuffixes directly (not just
! VnSuffixes): "pigiaqtitaq" chains vv-suffix into vv-suffix directly
! (giaq -> tit).
++giaq+1vv:giaq VerbContinuations ;

! "tit"/1vv ("to cause s.o. to do s.t."): Suffixes.csv's V/k/q-form is a
! single clean candidate (Neutral, bare "tit"), confirmed correct before
! "si"/1vv ("pivalliatittinirmut" keeps the full "tit"). But specifically
! before "jaq"/1vn ("pigiaqtitaq" family), gold shows the reduced span
! "ti" -- "tit"+"taq" (jaq's own t/k/q-context literal) would double the
! "t" ("tittaq"), but gold wants "titaq". Not guessing a general "tt->t"
! degemination rule from this alone (Inuktitut geminate consonants are
! often phonemically real, so a blanket rule risks breaking legitimate
! ones elsewhere) -- instead "ti" is wired as its own literal candidate
! specifically on the path toward VnSuffixes (where jaq lives), same
! "different literal spellings for different following contexts" pattern
! as ut/usiq/liuq's own multi-candidate treatment above.
++tit+1vv:tit VerbContinuations ;
++tit+1vv:ti VerbContinuations ;

! Third literal, "tis" (own trailing t -> s), specifically on the path
! toward "sima"/1vv: "tukisinaliqtissimajuq" needs "tit"+"sima" to
! surface as "tissima" (own t assimilates toward the following s-initial
! suffix), same "different literal spellings for different following
! contexts" pattern as "ti" above -- not generalized into a blanket
! t->s rule from a single word, same caution already applied to "ti"'s
! own tt->t case.
++tit+1vv:tis VerbContinuations ;

! "qqau"/1vv: see "lauq"/1vv's comment above (shared investigation).
++qqau+1vv:SUPPRqqau VerbContinuations ;

! "tuq"/1vv ("prolonged action: for a long time"): "akiraqtuqtut" =
! {akiraq:akiraq/1v}{tuq:tuq/1vv}{tut:jut/tv-ger-3p} -- V/k/q-context all
! Neutral (single candidate, "tuq" itself unchanged, plain
! concatenation); only t-context is Suppression (single candidate too,
! but not needed by this word's q-final root, and would need its own
! marker scoped to t only -- the existing SUPPR marker deletes q/k/t
! uniformly, which would be WRONG here since this suffix's own k/q-context
! is Neutral, not Suppression -- deferred rather than reusing SUPPR
! incorrectly). Never continued into VvSuffixes at first -- only ever
! validated word-final-ish via TvEndings ("akiraqtuqtut"); fixed once
! "aviktursimajuni" needed tuq -> sima/1vv. Also gained a VnSuffixes
! continuation in pursuit of the "uuktutigilugu" family (uuk+tuq(1vv)+
! ti/uti(ut/1vn)+gi(1nv)+lugu) -- turned out NOT sufficient on its own:
! gold's span for ut/1vn here is "ti" (via {ti:ut/1vn}), a spelling
! this project's ut/1vn candidate set doesn't cover (not the r-prefix or
! q-prefix families implemented above -- possibly the CSV's unimplemented
! "guti" t-context candidate, itself contingent on tuq/1vv having its own
! t-context spelling change not yet investigated). Left unattempted
! rather than guessing a new ut/1vn candidate from a single word; the
! VnSuffixes continuation itself is harmless and kept since it's
! independently correct.
++tuq+1vv:tuq VerbContinuations ;

! "iqqaqtuivilirijikkut"/"iqqaqtuivilirijikkunnut" need tuq/1vv's own
! trailing q dropped before the antipassive marker "i"/1vv attaches --
! Suffixes.csv's own "antipassive" column on tuq/1vv's row literally
! names "i/1vv" as its antipassive-marking partner suffix (and i/1vv's
! own condPrec, "antipassive:i/1vv", references it right back), a
! genuine confirmed row-level linkage, not a guess -- confirmed via the
! real Java analyzer's own output before wiring both entries.
++tuq+1vv:tu VerbContinuations ;

! "uuktuutigilugu" (root "uuk", k-final) needs "tu" with its own k
! preserved, NOT assimilated to "uuttu" -- same KGUARD trick as
! juq/1vn's own "KGUARDtu" elsewhere in this file. Not decomposable by
! the real Java analyzer either (confirmed via --pipeline).
++tuq+1vv:KGUARDtu VerbContinuations ;

! "aviktursimajuni" (root "avik", k-final) needs the own-q->r "tur"
! spelling (free variant, not in any CSV context column, same shape as
! naq/1vv's own "nar") WITH KGUARD too -- this is the same word that
! looked blocked earlier this session before KGUARD existed; revisiting
! now that the mechanism is proven. Not decomposable by the real Java
! analyzer either (confirmed via --pipeline).
++tuq+1vv:KGUARDtur VerbContinuations ;

! "sima"/1vv: "titiraqsimajut" = {titi:titiq/1v}{raq:raq/1vv}
! {sima:sima/1vv}{jut:jut/tv-ger-3p}. V+k+q ALL Neutral (single
! candidate, plain "sima" unchanged in every context -- unlike most
! suffixes above, its q-context does NOT delete what precedes it,
! confirmed by rereading the CSV row carefully: q-action1="n", not "s").
! t-context is 2-way ambiguous ("sima sima"/"s n"), deferred. Never
! continued into VnSuffixes at first -- only ever validated via TvEndings
! ("titiraqsimajut"); the same word needs sima -> juq/1vn, fixed once
! that was noticed.
++sima+1vv:sima VerbContinuations ;

! "ma"/1vv ("to be in a state of") -- a much bigger cluster once chained:
! "kati"+"ma" = "to be meeting/assembled" backs an entire "katima*"
! family of gold words. Its two V-form candidates ("ma"/"uma") were
! initially treated as unresolvable free variation without checking
! whether they collide. Confirmed via gold they DON'T: "katimaji" (root
! "kati", vowel-final) uses bare "ma", but "aaqqiumainnarutinut" (root
! "aaqqik", ALSO vowel-final once its own k is handled) uses "uma" --
! same context, different roots, different literal spellings --
! textbook "wire both in parallel" case, same as ngani/ani and
! nganut/anut in NounEndings above. t/k/q-form (Suppression, both
! candidates) not attempted: no gold word in the reachable cluster needs
! it yet.
++ma+1vv:ma VerbContinuations ;
++ma+1vv:uma VerbContinuations ;

! "raq"/1vv ("prolonged/staged action"): same shape as juq/kkut/gaq/lik
! (Neutral/Suppression), reuses SUPPR. Shares its target example with
! "sima"/1vv above ("titiraqsimajut").
++raq+1vv:SUPPRraq VerbContinuations ;

! "limaaq"/2vv ("ceaselessly" -- a DIFFERENT morpheme than
! "limaaq"/1nn "inclusiveness: all of" in NnSuffixes above, same spelling
! but a distinct homograph/function): "uqalimaarniq" =
! {uqa:uqaq/1v}{limaar:limaaq/2vv}{niq:niq/2vn} -- full V/t/k/q, same
! Neutral/Suppression shape, reuses SUPPR. The surface "limaar" (not
! "limaaq") comes entirely from "niq"'s own already-implemented
! Nasalization q-context (q->r), not from anything new here.
++limaaq+2vv:SUPPRlimaaq VerbContinuations ;

! "nga"/1vv: "turaangajuq" = {turaa:turaaq/1v}{nga:nga/1vv}
! {juq:juq/1vn} -- same shape as juq/kkut/gaq/raq (single candidate,
! Neutral/Suppression), reuses SUPPR unchanged.
++nga+1vv:SUPPRnga VerbContinuations ;

! Endings_verb.csv has ~72 "tv,imp" (imperative mood) rows (9
! intransitive "nsp" person/number combinations, plus 63 transitive "sp"
! subject+object combinations) -- initially looked like a large, mostly
! Voicing/Fusion-shaped family worth its own pass, same lever as "lu"/1q.
! But a full sweep of the 985-word gold standard found only TWO words
! anywhere using ANY imperative ending: "tunngasugit" (git/tv-imp-2s) and
! "tunngasugitsi" (gipsi/tv-imp-2p) -- Hansard parliamentary transcripts
! essentially never contain direct commands, so this family's CSV row
! count wildly overstates its real marginal value in THIS corpus
! (contrast Lever A's endings, each independently backed by many gold
! words). Implemented only what's cleanly gold-attested: "suk"/1vv (root
! "tunnga", V-context Neutral, its t/k-context Suppression is unrelated
! to and unaffected by the PMARK-scope issue that blocks
! "quviasukpunga" -- that collision is specifically about suk's own k
! assimilating incorrectly before a PMARK-derived p, which never arises
! here) and "git"/tv-imp-2s (k-context, Fusion == SUPPR reused, deletes
! suk's own trailing k, see TvEndings below): "tunngasu"+"git" =
! "tunngasugit". "gipsi"/tv-imp-2p is NOT implemented: its CSV k-form is
! literally "gipsi" (Fusion, single candidate), but the gold surface for
! "tunngasugitsi" is "...gitsi", not "...gipsi" -- a p->t-before-s
! alternation this row doesn't explain and no other CSV evidence
! confirms, so implementing it would mean guessing a new rule from one
! word, against this project's standing policy. The other 7 clean
! intransitive rows (langa/1s, li/3s, luk/1d, lik/3d, lit/3p -- all
! single-candidate V and t/k/q-Voicing, mechanically identical to
! "lu"/1q) and the entire 63-row transitive/object-agreement family are
! NOT implemented either: zero gold attestation for any of them in this
! corpus, and building them without a single real word to verify against
! would break from this project's standing "verify against a real gold
! example" discipline -- flagged as a scope/value question rather than
! silently either skipping the whole mood or guessing the rest.
++suk+1vv:suk VerbContinuations ;

! "quviasukpunga" needs suk/1vv's OWN t/k-context Suppression candidate
! (Suffixes.csv gives k-form "suk"/action1 "s" directly) -- only the
! V-context plain candidate above was ever wired, since the row's
! condPrec ("type:v,intransinfix:suk/1vv") is a grammatical-feature
! condition generate_affixes.py's bulk sweep doesn't model, so this row
! was always hand-authored, just incompletely.
++suk+1vv:SUPPRsuk VerbContinuations ;

LEXICON TvEndings

! "mat"/tv-caus-4s: Endings_verb.csv's "mat" row gives its V-context TWO
! space-separated action candidates, "i(ng)" and "i(m)" (Insertion of
! "ng" vs "m") -- but unlike a normal unresolvable ambiguity, checking
! every gold-attested vowel-final example ("summat" = su+mat,
! "uqaqqaummat" = ...qqau+mat, "uqaqsimammat" = ...sima+mat,
! "taimannaummat" = ...u+mat) shows ALL of them need "i(m)" and NONE need
! "i(ng)" -- so only "i(m)" is implemented; "i(ng)" is left unguessed (no
! gold word needs it in this corpus). The insertion never varies by what
! specific vowel precedes (same "su" ends in one vowel, "qqau"/
! "taimannau" end in two, both still take plain "m"), so it's
! unconditional-on-vowel-class -- a NEW marker (MINSERT, phonology.
! xfscript) rather than reusing VVNG, since VVNG's own condition is
! specifically "two preceding vowels", which "summat" (one vowel)
! contradicts.
!
! k/q-final stems ("uqalaurmat" = ...laur+mat, lauq's OWN trailing q)
! need the EXISTING NASAL marker (k->ng, q->r) -- confirmed by the CSV's
! own k-form/q-form actions for this row both being "nas". Stacked as
! NASALMINSERTmat (NASAL resolves first, deleting itself either way;
! only THEN does MINSERT check what's now immediately before it, so a
! q-that-became-r correctly reads as a consonant and blocks the
! m-insertion -- same "must run after upstream marker resolution"
! ordering discipline as VVNG's own comment above).
!
! t-final stems ("qanuimmat" = qanuit/1v's own t -> m, "taimaimmat"
! same) need a THIRD mechanism: a general unmarked "t -> m" rule
! (phonology.xfscript, same family as the existing t->n/k->t/p->t
! total-regressive-assimilation rules), placed at the very end so it
! only fires once both markers above have already resolved and literal
! "mat"'s own "m" is truly adjacent. "imaimmat" (root "ima", tagged 1a)
! is NOT attempted: the Kotlin gold standard's own comment on this word
! says the original iutools analyzer couldn't decompose it either ("ima"
! isn't a known root) -- not a genuine V-context target.
++mat+tv-caus-4s:NASALMINSERTmat # ;

! "mata"/tv-caus-4p: Endings_verb.csv's row is the plural sibling of
! "mat"/tv-caus-4s directly above -- same V-form action pair ("i(ng)"/
! "i(m)", same "i(m)" confirmed via gold: "amisuummata"/"qaujimammata"
! both need plain "m"), same t-form "a" (Assimilation, the general t->m
! rule above), same k-form/q-form "nas" (NASAL). Reuses the identical
! marker stack, just the literal's own trailing vowel differs.
++mata+tv-caus-4p:NASALMINSERTmata # ;

! "jara"/tv-ger-1s-3s ("I...it", 1s subject/3s object gerundive):
! Endings_verb.csv's V-context is a single clean candidate (Neutral,
! bare "jara"); every gold example in this cluster attaches to a
! vowel-final stem. t/k/q-form ("tara", also Neutral -- own literal
! spelling, not the general j->t rule, though it'd give the same result)
! not attempted: unattested in this corpus.
++jara+tv-ger-1s-3s:jara # ;

! "tillugit"/tv-part-3p (participle, 3rd person plural object, no
! specific subject) -- clean single V-context candidate per
! Endings_verb_participle.csv (Neutral, bare "tillugit"), needed by
! "katimatuinnaqtillugit" (tuinnaq/1vv -> tillugit directly).
++tillugit+tv-part-3p:tillugit # ;

++jut+tv-ger-3p:jut # ;

! "makkuktut" (root "makkuk", k-final) needs the bulk-generated "tut"
! (j->t already converted) with its own preceding k preserved, NOT
! assimilated to "makkuttut" -- same KGUARD trick as juq/1vn's
! "KGUARDtu" above. Not decomposable by the real Java analyzer either
! (confirmed via --pipeline).
++jut+tv-ger-3p:KGUARDtut # ;

! "junga"/tv-ger-1s: "quviattunga" = {quviat:quviak/1v}
! {tunga:junga/tv-ger-1s} -- identical V/t/k/q shape to "jut"/tv-ger-3p
! above: all single-candidate Neutral, reuses the existing
! j->t-after-t/k/q rule unchanged, no new mechanism at all.
++junga+tv-ger-1s:junga # ;

! "lugu"/tv-part-1s-3s-prespas and "lugit"/tv-part-1s-3p-prespas:
! "isumagillugu" = {isuma:isuma/1n}{gi:gi/1nv}{llugu:lugu/tv-part-1s-3s-
! prespas} and "katillugit" = {kati:kati/1v}{llugit:lugit/tv-part-1s-3p-
! prespas}. V-context only (both dialect variants in
! Endings_verb_participle.csv agree: V-form is the bare morpheme text with
! action "i(l)" -- Insertion of "l" -- UNCONDITIONALLY, not gated by
! anything the way VVNG's insertion is). Since this insertion never varies
! by what precedes in the V-context, it's baked directly into the literal
! lower-side text ("llugu"/"llugit", canonical "lugu"/"lugit") rather than
! implemented as a rule -- no marker needed. t/k/q-contexts differ by
! dialect (North Baffin vs Cumberland Peninsula use different forms) and
! aren't attempted.
++lugu+tv-part-1s-3s-prespas:llugu # ;

! "lugu"/tv-part-1s-3s-fut: same V-context "l"-insertion shape as the
! prespas sibling above (baked-in "llugu", unconditional insertion, no
! marker). Additionally needed a SUPPR-prefixed variant for
! consonant-final stems: "malillugu" (root "malik", k-final) -- gold
! shows the preceding k simply deleted, "mali"+"llugu", not converted via
! VOICE despite the CSV's k-form action reading "son" (Voicing) --
! trusted the empirical gold string over the CSV action code here, same
! "gold overrides a misleading CSV cell" precedent as several suffixes in
! this file.
++lugu+tv-part-1s-3s-fut:llugu # ;
++lugu+tv-part-1s-3s-fut:SUPPRllugu # ;

++lugit+tv-part-1s-3p-prespas:llugit # ;

! "maliktugit" (root "malik", k-final) needs a THIRD spelling, "tugit"
! (own leading "l" converted to "t" -- not the general j->t rule, which
! only affects j; a separate, unexplained "l"->"t" alternation of this
! suffix's own literal, same free-variant-spelling category as
! lutik/tv-part-3p-prespas's own "sutik" (l->s) sibling), PLUS KGUARD
! protection since the resulting k/t boundary would otherwise assimilate
! into "malittugit". Not decomposable by the real Java analyzer either
! (confirmed via --pipeline).
++lugit+tv-part-1s-3p-prespas:KGUARDtugit # ;

! "lugit"/tv-part-1s-3p-fut: same V-context "l"-insertion shape as
! "lugu"/tv-part-1s-3s-fut above, plus the same SUPPR-prefixed variant
! for consonant-final stems ("malillugit", root "malik", k-final -- same
! shape as "malillugu" above).
++lugit+tv-part-1s-3p-fut:llugit # ;
++lugit+tv-part-1s-3p-fut:SUPPRllugit # ;

! "lunga"/tv-part-1s-prespas (intransitive, no object): Endings_verb_
! participle.csv's V-form action is the same unmarked "i(l)" insertion
! as lugu/lugit's own V-context above, baked directly into the literal.
! Needed for "ministaullunga"/"qaujimallunga" (both vowel-final stems).
++lunga+tv-part-1s-prespas:llunga # ;

! "luta"/tv-part-1p-prespas (intransitive, no object): same shape as
! "lunga" directly above. Needed for "gavamaulluta".
++luta+tv-part-1p-prespas:lluta # ;

! "lutik"/tv-part-3p-prespas (intransitive, no object): V-context follows
! the same "i(l)" shape as its siblings above ("llutik"), but
! "katitsutik" (root "katit", t-final) needs a SEPARATE t-context literal
! ("sutik") the CSV's own "&utik"-placeholder cell doesn't spell out
! directly -- trusted the empirical gold surface over the ambiguous CSV
! notation, same precedent as "malillugu"'s own SUPPR variant above.
++lutik+tv-part-3p-prespas:llutik # ;
++lutik+tv-part-3p-prespas:sutik # ;

! "vugut"/tv-dec-1p: "niriuppugut" = {niriup:niriuk/1v}
! {pugut:vugut/tv-dec-1p} -- V-context Neutral (plain "vugut"); t/k-context
! both rewrite the suffix's own initial "v" to "p" (same PMARK mechanism
! as "vunga"/tv-dec-1s below, reused unchanged: v->p scoped by PMARK,
! plus the stem's own final consonant assimilates to match,
! "niriuk"->"niriup"). q-context is a genuinely different ambiguous
! 2-candidate case ("pugut qugut"), skipped -- NOTE: the more "obvious"
! example word "angiqpugut" (root "angiq", q-final) actually needs this
! blocked q-context, not the clean k-context the CSV row's k-form gives
! -- caught by checking which context the root's own final letter
! actually selects, not just eyeballing the surface.
++vugut+tv-dec-1p:vPMARKugut # ;

! "vunga"/tv-dec-1s: "nikuvippunga" = {nikuvip:nikuvik/1v}
! {punga:vunga/tv-dec-1s} -- V-context Neutral (plain "vunga"); t/k-context
! both rewrite the suffix's own initial "v" to "p" (Assimilation, single
! candidate "punga" in both) -- same *shape* as the j->t rule (a direct
! letter-triggered rewrite) but v->p instead of j->t, triggered by [t|k]
! not [t|k|q] (q-context is a genuinely different, ambiguous 2-candidate
! case: "punga qunga", skipped).
!
! UNLIKE j->t, this one needs a marker (PMARK, phonology.xfscript): a
! blank "v -> p || [t|k] _" would be the ONLY v-initial morpheme in this
! lexicon, so it would work by accident -- but the SECOND effect visible
! in the target word (the stem's own final consonant also assimilates,
! "nikuvik"->"nikuvip", not "nikuvikpunga" -- same shape as the general
! t->n rule, just k->p instead of t->n, triggered by the newly-rewritten
! "p") is NOT safe to write as a blanket "k -> p || _ p": root "makpiq"
! has its own internal "kp" cluster, and "makpigaq" (see "gaq"/1vn's
! comment in VnSuffixes above) already validated that this "k" must NOT
! change in that word. PMARK scopes both rewrites to
! specifically-this-suffix's-own-"p", not any "p" that happens to follow
! a "k".
!
! q-context deferred as noted; t-context's stem-side assimilation (if
! any) is unconfirmed by any gold example in this lexicon and not
! guessed at.
++vunga+tv-dec-1s:vPMARKunga # ;

! "vuq"/tv-dec-3s (declarative, 3rd person singular): same shape as
! vunga/vugut above: V-context Neutral (plain "vuq"), t/k-context reuses
! the EXISTING PMARK mechanism unchanged ("naammappuq" = "naamak"+
! PMARK(v->p, k->p)+"uq"). q-context needed one more literal candidate,
! "puq": Endings_verb.csv gives TWO q-context options (puq/Neutral,
! quq/Voicing) -- same ambiguity shape that left vunga/vugut's own
! q-context deferred -- but "nuqqaqpuq" attests "puq" specifically, so
! only that one candidate is wired (as its own literal, NOT by widening
! PMARK's v->p trigger to include q, which would also affect
! vunga/vugut's still-deferred ambiguity).
++vuq+tv-dec-3s:vuq # ;
++vuq+tv-dec-3s:vPMARKuq # ;
++vuq+tv-dec-3s:puq # ;

! Four more tv-endings:
!   - "jugut"/tv-ger-1p ("angiqtugut"): same shape as jut/junga/jutit
!     (all single-candidate Neutral, V-form "jugut" literal, q-context
!     "tugut" falls out of the existing j->t rule for free -- no new
!     marker).
!   - "jutit"/tv-ger-2s ("qujannamiingujutit"): same shape again, reached
!     via "u"/1nv's own TvEndings continuation above.
!   - "gama"/tv-caus-1s, "gapta"/tv-caus-1p, "gavit"/tv-caus-2s
!     ("qaujimagama"/"qaujimagatta"/"qaujimagavit"): Endings_verb.csv's
!     "caus" rows are single-candidate Neutral in the V-context (root
!     "qaujima" is vowel-final, so only V-context is exercised);
!     t/k/q-contexts differ per ending (some Assimilation, one
!     "rama"/Fusion -- an unbuilt mechanism) and aren't attempted here,
!     matching this project's minimal-scope policy of only wiring the
!     context an actual gold word needs.
++jugut+tv-ger-1p:jugut # ;
++jutit+tv-ger-2s:jutit # ;
++gama+tv-caus-1s:gama # ;

! "uqaqqaugamailaak" needs "gama"/tv-caus-1s to ALSO reach QParticles
! (ilaak/1e's own enclitic can follow a fully-inflected verb, same
! established pattern as "ga"/tn-nom-s-1s etc above on the noun side).
++gama+tv-caus-1s:gama QParticles ;
++gapta+tv-caus-1p:gapta # ;
++gavit+tv-caus-2s:gavit # ;

! "git"/tv-imp-2s: see "suk"/1vv's comment in VvSuffixes above for the
! full imperative-mood investigation. k-context, Fusion == SUPPR reused,
! deletes suk's own trailing k: "tunngasu"+"git" = "tunngasugit".
++git+tv-imp-2s:git # ;
++git+tv-imp-2s:SUPPRgit # ;

! "gipsi"/tv-imp-2p ("tunngasugitsi"): the CSV's own k-form is literally
! "gipsi" (Fusion), but the gold surface is "...gitsi", not "...gipsi"
! -- an unexplained p->t-before-s alternation this row doesn't document
! and no other CSV evidence confirms (see "suk"/1vv's own comment in
! VvSuffixes for the fuller investigation history). Trusted the
! empirical gold surface directly as its own literal, same "wire what's
! evidenced, don't generalize a rule from one word" precedent used
! throughout this session -- not decomposable by the real Java analyzer
! either (confirmed via --pipeline).
++gipsi+tv-imp-2p:SUPPRgitsi # ;
